2 CONT a)     '''    MARGARITA d’Alneto '''(-[after 9 Dec 1342]).  Campanile names “Margarita d’Alneto, unica figliuola di Roberto d’Alneto Signor di Carinola, di Teano, di Cassano, di Caramanico” and records her two marriages (no source
2 CONC s cited)[902].  Camera notes that I registri angioini name Margherita as “unigenita filia quond. nobilis domini Roberti de Alneto”[903].  "Bertrand de Baux de Berre duc d’Andrie" received a proxy from “Marguerite d’Aulnay son épou
2 CONC se”, which he presented to “Benoit Ruffo, juge de la ville d’Aversa”, by charter dated [1332/33][904].  Her two marriages are confirmed by the following document: a charter dated 1305 [presumably misdated: 1335?] records a royal c
2 CONC ommission obtained by “Bertrand des Beaux chevalier Comte de Montescagens et Marg. Daunay sa femme, avant veuve de Louis de Flandre chevalier” against “la Dame de Cassel” confirming revenue from “l’Espier de Bergues” as dower assi
2 CONC gned to Marguerite, a decision of the parlement de Paris dated 9 Dec 1342 relating to the same matter[905]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly LOUIS de Flandre, son of PHILIPPE de Flandre Conte di Teano & his second wife Philippa de Milly ([1305/07]-after 15 Jul 1311).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (1324) as his second wife, BERTRAND de Baux Conti di Andria, son of BERTRAND de Baux Seigneur de Berre, Barone di Trogessana & his wife --- (-Naples 1351 bur Naples). 
2 CONT
