1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulcentw.htm#BetrandLevisdiedafter1382
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.      '''   BERTRAND [I] de Lévis ''' (-after 1382).  “Beatrix vicomtesse de Lautrec” promised not to dispose of her assets without the consent of “ses fils...Philippe et Bertrand de Lévis”, with the consent of “...vicomte Guill
2 CONC aume cousin de lad. dame”, by charter dated 28 Nov 1326, and committed to pay certain sums to her sons “pro custodia castri [de La Focz]” where she was living by charter dated 29 May 1327[464].  “Beatrix vic. de Lautrec” ordered h
2 CONC er subjects to swear allegiance to “nos fils Philippe et à Bertrand” by charter dated 21 Mar 1335 (O.S.)[465].  Seigneur de Florensac.  "Guigues sire de Roche vicomte de Lautrec" named "Bertrand de Levis chevalier seigneur de Flor
2 CONC ensac son oncle" proxy to receive homage by charter dated 9 Sep 1356[466].  The testament of "Guigue seigneur de Roche et de Posquières chevalier vicomte de Lautrec", dated 24 Apr 1366, named “son fils Philippe” as his universal h
2 CONC eir, with “son frère Bertrand de Lévis...son oncle Bertrand de Lévis seigneur de Florensac” as successive substitutes[467].  Père Anselme records his testament dated 1382[468]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1336 or before) JOURDAINE de Roche-en-Régnier, daughter of GUIGUES [III] Seigneur de Roche-en-Régnier & his second wife Guyotte de Posquières Dame de Bellegarde et de Broussan.  Père Anselme records her parentage and marr
2 CONC iage “dès l’an 1336”)[469].  The primary source which confirms the information has not been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Bertrand [I] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT --------
