1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caterina_di_Taranto
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/277171534/caterina-di_chiaramonte
2 CONT
2 CONT Caterina del Balzo Orsini, married  1415 Bartolomeo Tristano di Chiaramonte (de Clermont) who was created Count of Copertino (1380 - c. 1432) son of Déodat II de Guilhem, seigneur de Clermont-Lodève.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She was daughter of Mary of Enghien and Raimondo Orsini del Balzo di Nola and sister of Giovanni Antonio Orsini del Balzo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her early life was tumultuous; her father Raimondo was assassinated in 1406 after being encouraged by Pope Innocent VII to rebel against King Ladislaus. Caterina's mother continued to fight, and for months held Taranto against Lad
2 CONC islaus. However, Ladislaus prevailed, and forced Mary to marry him, by imprisoning her and her children until she submitted to the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT On her death in 1429 Count Tristan divided the inheritance between his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raymond de Clermont (Raimondello di Chiaromonte), 2 Count of Copertino died on 2 March 1443, leaving his inheritance to his sister Sancia;
2 CONT Sancia died 30 March 1468 ,3 Countess of Copertino who married Francesco II del Balzo, 3 Duke of Andria 1410-1482
2 CONT Margherita, who married Antonio Ventimiglia, Marquess of Geraci.
2 CONT Isabella 1424-1465 who married Ferdinand I of Aragon, King of Naples
