1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard Grey, 3rd Earl of Kent .
2 CONT * Born	1481
2 CONT * Died	May 3, 1524 (aged 42-43)
2 CONT * Father	George Grey, 2nd Earl of Kent
2 CONT * Mother	Anne Woodville
2 CONT * Spouse(s)	Elizabeth Hussey, Margaret Fynche
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created a Knight of the Garter in 1505, alongside the latter Henry Stafford, 1st Earl of Wiltshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard wound up heavily in debt, probably through gambling, and was forced to alienate most of his property. A good part ended up in the crown's hands; historians disagree regarding what this says about the relationship of Henry 
2 CONC VII of England with the aristocracy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard died childless and was succeeded as earl by his half-brother Henry. Henry tried, with little success, to reacquire the property Richard had sold, and had to live as a modest gentleman, never formally taking title as earl.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links 
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Grey,_3rd_Earl_of_Kent
