2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''Elizabeth STAFFORD (C. Sussex)
2 CONT *''''''Died: BEF 11 May 1532
2 CONT *''''''Buried: 11 May 1532, Boreham, Essex, England
2 CONT *''''''Notes: was at court as one of Elizabeth of York's ladies by 1494. On 23 Jul 1505 she married Robert Radcliffe, Lord Fitzwalter, who was created Earl of Sussex in 1529. It was as Lady Fitzwalter, however, that she was at the
2 CONC  court of Henry VIII. She did not stay long. In May of 1510, after she informed her brother the Duke of Buckingham that their younger and newly married sister, Anne, was being courted by the King, the King himself forced Queen Cat
2 CONC alina to dismiss Elizabeth Fitzwalter from her service. She was, however, in attendance at the Field of Cloth of Gold in 1520. 
2 CONT *Father: Henry STAFFORD (2° D. Buckingham)
2 CONT *Mother: Catherine WOODVILLE (D. Buckingham/D. Bedford)
2 CONT *''''''Married: Robert RADCLIFFE (1° E. Sussex) 23 Jul 1505
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Henry RADCLIFFE (2° E. Sussex)
2 CONT **2. George RADCLIFFE
2 CONT **3. Humphrey RADCLIFFE
2 CONT **4. Thomas RADCLIFFE 
2 CONT *http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STAFFORD1.htm#Elizabeth STAFFORD (C. Sussex)
2 CONT *_________________
