1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sometime before the coronation of Elizabeth in May 1465, Catherine was married with Henry Stafford, 2nd Duke of Buckingham; both were still children. A contemporary description of Elizabeth Woodville's coronation r
2 CONC elates that Catherine, and her husband were carried on squires' shoulders. According to Dominic Mancini, Buckingham resented his marriage to a woman of inferior birth. The couple, had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Edward Stafford, 3rd Duke of Buckingham (3 February 1478 – 17 May 1521) 
2 CONT # Elizabeth Stafford, Countess of Sussex (ca. 1479 – 11 May 1532) 
2 CONT # Henry Stafford, 3rd Earl of Wiltshire (c. 1479 – 6 April 1523) 
2 CONT # '''Anne Stafford''', Countess of Huntingdon (c. 1483–1544)
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stafford-351
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LR2R-ZDT
2 CONT * http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/Bios/CatherineWoodville%28DBuckingham%29.htm
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Hastings,_Countess_of_Huntingdon
2 CONT * http://www.kateemersonhistoricals.com/TudorWomenWi-Z.htm ___________________________
2 CONT *'''Anne Stafford1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8
2 CONT *'''F, #27358, d. after 24 March 1544
2 CONT *Father     Sir Henry Stafford, 2nd Duke Buckingham, 7th Earl of Stafford, 8th Lord Stafford2,3,4,5,9,8 b. 4 Sep 1455, d. 2 Nov 1483
2 CONT *Mother     Katherine Wydeville2,3,4,9 b. c 1458, d. 18 May 1497
2 CONT *'''     Anne Stafford married Sir Walter Herbert, son of Sir William Herbert, 1st Earl Pembroke, 1st Lord Herbert, Sheriff of Glamorgan & Morgan Nock, Chief Justice of North & South Wales and Anne Devereux, circa 1490.2,4,6,7 Ann
2 CONC e Stafford married Sir George Hastings, 1st Earl Huntingdon, 3rd Lord Hastings, High Steward of the Honor of Leicester, of Launde Convent, & of Burton-on-Trent Abbey, son of Sir Edward Hastings, 2nd Lord Hastings, Constable of Lei
2 CONC cester Castle, High Forester of Southwood and Mary Hungerford, circa December 1509; They had 5 sons (Sir Francis, 2nd Earl of Huntingdon; Sir Thomas; Sir Edward, Lord Hastings of Loughborough, Master of the Horse; Henry; & William
2 CONC ) and 3 daughters (Dorothy, wife of Sir Richard Devereux; Mary, wife of Sir Thomas, 6th Lord Berkeley; & Katherine).2,3,4,5,6,7,8 Anne Stafford died after 24 March 1544; Buried at Stoke Poges, Buckinghamshire.2,4,7
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Sir Walter Herbert b. c 1458, d. 16 Sep 1507
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Sir George Hastings, 1st Earl Huntingdon, 3rd Lord Hastings, High Steward of the Honor of Leicester, of Launde Convent, & of Burton-on-Trent Abbey b. c 1486, d. 24 Mar 1544
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Dorothy Hastings+10 b. c 1511
2 CONT **Sir Francis Hastings, 2nd Earl Huntingdon, 4th Lord Hastings, Lt. Gen. & Chief Captain of the army and fleet for service abroad, Constable of Conway Castle, Lord Lt. of counties Rutland, Leicester, Derby, & Warwick+2,4,7 b. c 15
2 CONC 14, d. 23 Jun 1560
2 CONT **Sir Thomas Hastings, Sheriff of Warwickshire & Leicestershire, Justice of the Peace for Leicestershire11,4,5,7,8 b. c 1515
2 CONT **Mary Hastings12,2 b. c 1518, d. Mar 1533
2 CONT **Sir Edward Hastings, Baron Hastings of Loughborough13 b. c 1520, d. 5 Mar 1572
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S8469] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. VI, p. 655; The Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles, by Gerald Paget, Vol. 2, p. 179; Plantagenet Ancestry of 17th Century Colonists, by David Faris, p. 135
2 CONC ; Burke's Peerage, 1938, p. 1357.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 387.
2 CONT * 3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 675.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 374.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 378.
2 CONT * 6.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 85.
