1 NAME Jean /de La Tour d'Auvergne/
2 GIVN Jean
2 _MARNM de La Tour d'Auvergne
1 NAME Jean III, comte d'Auvergne et de Boulogne
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1467
2 PLAC Paris, France
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 MAR 1501
1 OCCU Giovanni III de La Tour, Conte d'Alvernia e di Lauraguais
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John III of Auvergne (1467 – 28 March 1501), Count of Auvergne, Count of Boulogne, Count de Lauraguais, was the son''' of Bertrand VI, Count of Auvergne and Louise de La Trémoille (1432 – 10 April 1474), Dame de
2 CONC  Boussac, the daughter of Georges de la Trémoille. '''He was the last in the male line of Counts of Auvergne from the La Tour d'Auvergne family.'''
2 CONT Family and children
2 CONT '''John married Jeanne de Bourbon-Vendôme''', daughter of Jean VIII, Count of Vendôme,[1] and Isabelle, Dame de la Roche-sur-Yon, '''on 11 January 1495. They had:'''
2 CONT 1. Anne,[2] married John Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany.
2 CONT 2. Madeleine, married Lorenzo II, Duke of Urbino.[1]
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_IV,_Count_of_Auvergne
2 CONT '''John III of Auvergne'''
2 CONT '''Born	1467'''
2 CONT '''Died	28 March 1501 (aged 33–34)'''
2 CONT '''Orléans'''
2 CONT Noble family	La Tour d'Auvergne
2 CONT '''Spouse(s)	Jeanne de Bourbon-Vendôme'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Bertrand VI, Count of Auvergne
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Louise de La Trémoille
2 CONT _________
2 CONT '''Jean III de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne'''1 
2 CONT M, #108297, '''b. circa 1467, d. 28 March 1501'''
2 CONT Last Edited=30 Jun 2020
2 CONT '''     Jean III de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne was born circa 1467. He was the son of''' Bernard VI de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne and Louise de la Trémoille.2 '''He married Jeanne de Bourbon''', daughter of Jean II de Bourbon, Comte
2 CONC  de Vendôme and Isabel de Beauveau, '''on 11 January 1495.3 He died on 28 March 1501'''.3
2 CONT '''     He gained the title of Comte d'Auvergne. He gained the title of Comte de Boulogne.1 He gained the title of Comte de Lauranguais'''.1
2 CONT '''Children of Jean III de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne and Jeanne de Bourbon'''
2 CONT 1. Madeleine de la Tour+4 d. 23 Apr 1519
2 CONT 2. Anne de la Tour, Comtesse d'Auvergne1 b. a 1495, d. Jun 1524
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 236. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT 2.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinc
2 CONC t or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 81. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT 3.[S130] Wikipedia, online http;//www.wikipedia.org. Hereinafter cited as Wikipedia.
2 CONT 4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 82.
2 CONT https://thepeerage.com/p10830.htm#i108297
2 CONT _______
2 CONT '''Jean I, Sire de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne, Lauraguais, & Boulogne'''1,2,3,4
2 CONT Last Edited	27 May 2013
2 CONT M, #57498, '''b. 1467, d. 28 March 1501'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Bertrand VI, Sire de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne & Boulogne2 d. 26 Sep 1494
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Louise de la Tremoille2 d. 10 Apr 1474
2 CONT '''     Jean I, Sire de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne, Lauraguais, & Boulogne was born in 1467.1,2 A contract for the marriage of Jean I, Sire de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne, Lauraguais, & Boulogne and Jeanne 'the Beautiful' de Bourbon 
2 CONC was signed on 2 January 1495.1,2,3,4 Jean I, Sire de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne, Lauraguais, & Boulogne died on 28 March 1501.'''1,2
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Jeanne 'the Beautiful' de Bourbon''' b. c 1465, d. 22 Jan 1512
