1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Anne de la Tour1 
2 CONT *''''''F, d. 13 October 1512
2 CONT *Father    Bertrand VI, Sire de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne & Boulogne2,3 d. 26 Sep 1494
2 CONT *Mother    Louise de la Tremoille2,3 d. 10 Apr 1474
2 CONT *''''''     A contract for the marriage of Anne de la Tour and Alexander Stewart, Earl of March, Mar, Garioch; Duke of Albany was signed on 16 January 1479 at France.2,4 Anne de la Tour married Louis de Seyssel, Comte de la Chambr
2 CONC e, son of Amédée Aymon de Seyssel, Vicomte de Maurienne, Comte de la Chambre, de Léville, & Dammartin and Marie de Savoy, on 15 February 1487.2,5 Anne de la Tour died on 13 October 1512 at La Rochette, Savoy, Italy.6,2
2 CONT *''''''Family 1     Louis de Seyssel, Comte de la Chambre b. 1450, d. 7 May 1517
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **◦Jean Charles de la Chambre, Baron & Seigneur de Sermoyé+5,2 d. a 5 Dec 1565
2 CONT *''''''Family 2     Alexander Stewart, Earl of March, Mar, Garioch; Duke of Albany b. c 1454, d. 1485
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **◦John Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany1 d. 2 Jun 1536
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. I, p. 80-81.
2 CONT * 2.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. X, Tafel 95.
2 CONT * 3.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. I, p. 80.
2 CONT * 4.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. I, Tafel 80-81.
2 CONT * 5.[S33] Leo van de Pas: Genealogics.org.
2 CONT * 6.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. I, p. 81.
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1834.htm#i55113
2 CONT *_____________
2 CONT *''''''Anne de la Tour1 
2 CONT *''''''F, #103504, d. 13 October 1512
2 CONT *Last Edited=23 May 2008
2 CONT *''''''     Anne de la Tour was the daughter of Bernard VI de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne and Louise de la Trémoille.2 She married, firstly, Alexander Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany, son of James II Stewart, King of Scotland and Marie 
2 CONC von Geldern, between 16 January 1479 and 4 December 1479 at France.1 She married, secondly, Louis de la Chambre, Comte de la Chambre on 17 May 1487 at Savoy, France.3 She married by contract, firstly, Alexander Stewart, 1st Duke o
2 CONC f Albany, son of James II Stewart, King of Scotland and Marie von Geldern, on 16 January 1478/79.1 She married by contract, secondly, Louis de la Chambre, Comte de la Chambre on 15 February 1486/87.1 She died on 13 October 1512 at
2 CONC  La Rochette Castle, Savoy, France.3 She was buried at Monastery of La Rochette, La Rochette, Savoy, France.2
2 CONT *''''''      From 16 January 1478/79, her married name became Stewart. From 15 February 1486/87, her married name became de la Chambre.1
2 CONT *''''''Child of Anne de la Tour and Alexander Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany
2 CONT ** 1.John Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany+ b. bt 1481 - 1485, d. 2 Jun 1536
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 79. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 235. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT * 3.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 81.
2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p10351.htm#i103504
2 CONT *_________________ Bertrand IV, sn de La Tour, +1423; m.11.1.1389 Marie d'Auvergne, Dame de Montgascon (+7.8.1437), dau.of Godefroy de Boulogne and Jeanne de Ventadour; They had issue: 
2 CONT *A1. Bertrand V, sn de La Tour et Montgascon, succeeded as Cte d'Auvergne & de Boulogne, +22.3.1461; m.1416 Jacquette du Peschin (+21.9.1473), dau.of Louis sn du Peschin and Ysoul de Sully, Dame de Varennes 
2 CONT **B1. Bertrand VI, Cte d'Auvergne et de Boulogne, *1417, +St.Saturnin 26.9.1494; m.30.1.1444 Louise de La Tremoille, Dame de Boussac (+10.4.1474) 
2 CONT ***C4. Anne, +13.10.1512; 1m: 16.1.1479 Alexander Stuart, Duke of Albany (+1485); 2m: 15.2.1487 Louis de Seyssel, Cte de La Chambre (+7.5.1517) 
2 CONT
