2 CONT *'''     Lady Cicely Grey was the daughter of Thomas Grey, 1st Marquess of Dorset and Cecilia Bonville, Baroness Bonville and Harington.1 She married John Sutton, 3rd Lord Dudley, son of Edward Sutton, 2nd Lord Dudley and Cicely W
2 CONC illoughby, after 30 October 1519.1 She died circa April 1554.1 She was buried on 28 April 1554 at St. Margaret's Church, Westminster, London, England.1
2 CONT *'''      From after 30 October 1519, her married name became de Sutton.
2 CONT *'''Children of Lady Cicely Grey and John Sutton, 3rd Lord Dudley
2 CONT ** 1.Edward Sutton, 4th Lord Dudley+1 d. 8 Jul 1586
2 CONT ** 2.Henry Dudley1
2 CONT ** 3.George Dudley1
2 CONT ** 4.Eleanor Sutton+1
2 CONT ** 5.Thomas Dudley+1 b. c 1539, d. c 1574
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 1, page 1192. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p264.htm#i2636 _________________
2 CONT *'''Cecily Grey1,2,3,4,5,6,7
2 CONT *'''F, #86885, b. circa 1488
2 CONT *Father      Sir Thomas Grey, 1st Marquess of Dorset, Lord Ferrers, Constable of the Tower of London & Ruthland Castle1,2,3,8,5,9,10 b. c 1455, d. 30 Aug 1501
2 CONT *Mother     Cecily Bonville1,2,3,8,5,9,10 b. 1461, d. 12 Apr 1530 or 12 May 1530
2 CONT *'''     Cecily Grey was born circa 1488 at of Groby, Leicestershire, England.1 She married Sir John Dudley, 3rd Lord Dudley, son of Sir Edward Sutton, 2nd Lord Dudley & Lord Powys and Cecily Willoughby, circa 1512; Betrothed befo
2 CONC re 30 October 1501. They had 4 sons (Sir Edward, 4th Lord Dudley; Sir Henry; Thomas; & Sir George) and 3 daughters (Margaret, wife of William Gibbons; Dorothy; & Elizabeth).1,2,3,4,5,6,7 Cecily Grey was buried on 28 April 1554 at 
2 CONC St. Margaret's Chapel, Westminster, London, Middlesex, England.1,2,5
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir John Dudley, 3rd Lord Dudley b. c 1496
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Sir Edward Dudley, 4th Lord Dudley+11 b. c 1513
2 CONT **Sir Henry Dudley+2 b. c 1517, d. bt 1568 - 1570
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. IV, p. 481.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 279-280.
2 CONT * 3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 359.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 306.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 157.
