2 NOTE Burials
3 CONT The chapel has been the site of many royal funerals and interments. Royals interred here include: 
3 CONT Altar 
3 CONT Edward IV, King of England, in 1483 
3 CONT Henry VI, King of England (reburial), in 1484 
3 CONT Elizabeth Woodville, Queen of England in 1492 
3 CONT Edward VII, King of the United Kingdom, in 1910 
3 CONT Alexandra of Denmark, Queen of the United Kingdom, in 1925
3 CONT Quire 
3 CONT Jane Seymour, Queen of England, in 1537 
3 CONT Henry VIII, King of England and Ireland, in 1547 
3 CONT Charles I, King of England, Scotland and Ireland, in 1649 
3 CONT Stillborn son of Queen Anne (last monarch of the House of Stuart), in 1698.
3 CONT Royal Vault 
3 CONT Princess Amelia of the United Kingdom in 1810 
3 CONT Princess Augusta, Duchess of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel, in 1813 
3 CONT Princess Charlotte of Wales in 1817 
3 CONT Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz, Queen of the United Kingdom, in 1818 
3 CONT George III, King of the United Kingdom, in 1820 
3 CONT Prince Edward, Duke of Kent and Strathearn, in 1820 
3 CONT Princess Elizabeth of Clarence in 1821 
3 CONT Prince Frederick, Duke of York and Albany, in 1827 
3 CONT George IV, King of the United Kingdom, in 1830 
3 CONT William IV, King of the United Kingdom in 1837 
3 CONT Princess Augusta Sophia of the United Kingdom in 1840 
3 CONT Adelaide of Saxe-Meiningen, Queen of the United Kingdom in 1849 
3 CONT Prince Adolphus, Duke of Cambridge in 1850 
3 CONT George V, King of Hanover, in 1878 
3 CONT Princess Augusta of Hesse-Cassel in 1889 
3 CONT Princess Mary Adelaide of Cambridge in 1897 
3 CONT Francis, Duke of Teck in 1900
3 CONT Near West Door 
3 CONT George V, King of the United Kingdom, in 1936 
3 CONT Mary of Teck, Queen of the United Kingdom in 1953 
3 CONT King George VI Memorial Chapel (North Nave Aisle) 
3 CONT George VI, King of the United Kingdom in 1952 
3 CONT Princess Margaret, Countess of Snowdon (ashes) in 2002 
3 CONT Elizabeth Bowes-Lyon, The Queen Mother, in 2002 
3 CONT Albert Memorial Chapel 
3 CONT Prince Leopold, Duke of Albany, in 1884 
3 CONT Prince Albert Victor, Duke of Clarence, in 1892
3 CONT Other 
