2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Tudor (daughter of Henry VII) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Henry VII 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother Elizabeth of York 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 2 July 1492(1492-07-02)
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 14 September 1495 (aged 3)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Chapel of St Edward the Confessor, Westminster Abbey 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Tudor (2 July 1492 – 14 September 1495) was the second daughter and fourth child of Henry VII of England and Elizabeth of York.
2 CONT
2 CONT A marriage to the French prince Francis (later Francis I) was being proposed when she died of atrophy, around six months before the birth of her sister Mary. Elizabeth was buried in Westminster Abbey in the Chapel of St. Edward th
2 CONC e Confessor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her older siblings were Arthur, Prince of Wales; Margaret; and the future Henry VIII. Her younger siblings were Mary; Edmund, Duke of Somerset; Edward Tudor; and Catherine.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth_Tudor_(daughter_of_Henry_VII)
2 CONT --------------------
