2 CONT *'''     Sir Thomas Stanley, 2nd Earl Derby, 3rd Lord Stanley, Lord Strange of Knockin Also Viscount Kynton, Lord Mohun, Basset, Burnal, Lacy and Lord of the Isle Man and Lord of the Isles.19,3 He was born before 1485.6,12 He and 
2 CONC Elizabeth Welles were engaged in March 1498; A dispensation for the marriage (as they were related in the 3rd and 4th degrees of consanquinity) was granted, but she died within the same year.3,6,7,8,12,14,15 A contract for the mar
2 CONC riage of Sir Thomas Stanley, 2nd Earl Derby, 3rd Lord Stanley, Lord Strange of Knockin and Anne Hastings was signed on 17 December 1505; They had 3 sons''' (John; Sir Edward, 3rd Earl Derby, Lord Strange; & Henry) '''and 1 daughte
2 CONC r''' (Margaret, wife of Sir Robert Radcliffe, 1st Earl of Sussex, Viscount FitzWalter).20,3,4,6,10,11,12 '''Sir Thomas Stanley, 2nd Earl Derby, 3rd Lord Stanley, Lord Strange of Knockin died on 23 May 1521 at Colham Green, Middles
2 CONC ex, England; Buried at Syon Monastery, Middlesex.3,6,12 His estate was probated on 27 June 1524.6,12
