2 CONT *Pg.143
2 CONT *   IBID. "Mr Halsoll."] Richard, son and heir of Henry and grandson of Sir Thomas Halsall of Halsall Knt., whose wife was Jane, '''daughter and coheiress of Sir John Stanley of Honford Knt. (base son and heir''' of John Stanley, 
2 CONC brother of Thomas first Earl of Derby) and of '''Elizabeth his wife, daughter and coheiress''' of Sir John Harrington of Hornby Castle Knt. and of his wife, the daughter and heiress of Sir Robert Nevile of Hornby. In her widowhood
2 CONC  Dame Jane Halsall married 2nd Edward VI. John Osbaldeston Esq., and in the same year her daughter Maud married Edward Osbaldeston of Osbaldeston, her husband's son by his first wife Margaret, 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/derbyhouseholdb00ffargoog#page/n264/mode/1up
2 CONT *daughter of George Lord Strange. The mother of Sir Thomas Halsall was Margaret, daughter of James Stanley, Clerk, and by her husband, Sir Henry Halsall of Halsall, she had issue six sons and three daughters. On the south side of 
2 CONC the chancel of Halsall Church upon an altar tomb ornamented with escutcheons, now defaced, are the full-length figures of a knight of the Halsalls and a lady of the Stanleys. (Baines, vol. iv, p. 262.) Richard Halsall Esq. succeed
2 CONC ed his father Henry (whose Will was proved at Chester 30th December 1574) and married before 1567 Ann, daughter of Alexander Barlow of Barlow Esq. M.P. the niece of Margaret Countess of Derby, and a lady who was a frequent visiter
2 CONC  at Knowsley, (See p. 106, Note.) By this lady he had no surviving issue, and the name of his second wife has not been recorded in the Visit. Lanc., A° 1613, c. 5, 50 b. in Coll. Arm. She was, however, Jane, daughter of William No
2 CONC rres and the mother of Sir Cuthbert Halsall, mentioned page 35 and afterwards in this Diary. (Lanc. MSS., vol. iii. pp. 216-331.)  ______________ Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Shropshire Walcot Family - Chart XII: Newton Family;
2 CONC  http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id106.html. (Steven Ferry, May 12, 2020.)
