2 CONT *'''Sir James Stanley1 
2 CONT *M, #13796
2 CONT *Last Edited=6 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT *'''     Sir James Stanley was the son of Sir George Stanley, Lord Strange (of Knokyn) and Joan Lestrange, Baroness Strange.1 He married Anne Hart, daughter of John Hart and Elizabeth Peache.1
2 CONT *'''     He held the office of Marshall of Ireland.1 He lived at Crosshall, Lancashire, England.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Sir James Stanley and Anne Hart
2 CONT ** 1.Sir George Stanley+1
2 CONT ** 2.Henry Stanley+2 b. 1515, d. 23 Jul 1598
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1102. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT * 2.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 1893.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p1380.htm#i13796
2 CONT *_________________
2 CONT *1. Sir George Stanley KG, jure uxoris Baron Strange (sum. to Parliament v.p. 15 Nov 1482 in his wife's Barony of Strange), Knight of the Bath 1475, Constable of Pontefract Castle and of Knaresborough Castle 1485 and of Wicklow Ca
2 CONC stle 1485/6, Chief Steward of the Duchy of Lancaster North of Trent 1486-97, Privy Councillor (b. c. 1460; dvp. 5 Dec 1497), mar. bef. 26 Feb 1481/2 Joan le Strange, suo jure Baroness Strange (of Knockin) and Baroness Mohun (d. 20
2 CONC  Mar 1513/4), only dau. and hrss. of John [le Strange], 8th Baron Strange (of Knockin) and 4th Baron Mohun, by his wife Lady Jacquetta Wydville, 5th dau. of Richard [Wydville], 1st Earl Rivers, and had issue:   .....
2 CONT **'''	3a. Hon Sir James Stanley, of Crosshall, co. Lancaster, Marshal of Ireland, mar. Anne Talbot (widow of Edmund Talbot, of Bashall, co. York), dau. of John Hart by his wife Elizabeth Peache, sister and hrss. of Sir John Peache
2 CONC , of Lullingstone Castle, co. Kent, and had issue:
2 CONT ***		1b. Sir George Stanley, Marshal of Ireland and Captain of the Isle of Man
2 CONT ***		2b. Henry Stanley, of Aughton (b. 1515; d. 23 Jul 1598), mar. 26 Sep 1563 Mary Stanley, only dau. and hrss. of Peter Stanley, of Bickerstaffe, co. Lancaster, 3rd son of Sir William Stanley, of Hooton, and had issue:  ....
2 CONT *From: http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/Derby1485.htm
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *'''James STANLEY of Crosshall (Esq. Marshall of Ireland)
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1481 
2 CONT *'''Notes: his wife had been previously married to Edmund Talbot, by whom she had a son, Sir Thomas Talbot (b. 1517 - d. 1558).  Anne was neice of the well known Sir John Peach (b. 1473 - d. 1522) who was a close personal friend o
2 CONC f Henry VIII and a well known jouster and soldier. Anne's brother, Sir Percival Hart (b. 1496 - d. 1580) was a Knight Harbinger and entertained Queen Elizabeth at his manor of Bark Hart near Orpington.  He was also close to Henry 
2 CONC VIII who stood godfather at his sons chrsitening. Sir James Stanley led a detachment of troops in the army of his nephew, Edward Stanley, 3º Earl of Derby, during the northern rebellion of 1536, as did Thomas Talbot (Anne's son by
2 CONC  her first marriage), who was Sir James' ward. Anne died 1566, buried Blackburn Parish Church. Sir James Stanley's exact date of death is unknown.  He was living as late as 1545 when he was steward of Burscough Priory.
2 CONT *Father: George STANLEY (B. Strange of Knockin)
2 CONT *Mother: Joan STRANGE (10° B. Strange of Knockin)
2 CONT *'''Married: Anne HART (b. ABT 1491 - d. 1566) (dau. of John Hart and Elizabeth Peache) (w. of Edmund Talbot of Bashall) 1510, Lullingstone, Kent, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. George STANLEY (Marshall of Ireland)
2 CONT **2. Henry STANLEY of Aughton (Esq.)
2 CONT **3. Alice STANLEY
2 CONT **4. Margaret STANLEY
2 CONT **5. Edward STANLEY (b. ABT 1526)
2 CONT **6. Thomas STANLEY (b. ABT 1528)
2 CONT **7. Jane STANLEY
2 CONT **8. Anne STANLEY
2 CONT **9. Eleanor (Helen) STANLEY 
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STANLEY4.htm#James STANLEY of Crosshall (Esq. Marshall of Ireland)
2 CONT *____________________
