1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Jane Neville1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9
2 CONT *'''F, #27360, b. circa 1493, d. between 4 June 1535 and 26 October 1538
2 CONT *Father     Sir George Neville, Lord Abergavenny, Constable of Dover Castle, Warden of the Cinque Ports2,3,10,5,6,11,8,9 b. c 1469
2 CONT *Mother     Joan FitzAlan2,3,10,6,11,9 b. c 1470, d. 14 Nov 1508
2 CONT *'''     Jane Neville was born circa 1493 at of Abergavenny, Monmouthshire, Wales.3 A contract for the marriage of Jane Neville and Sir Henry Pole, Lord Montague, High Steward of Tewkesbury Abbey & of Hornby Abbey was signed on 8 
2 CONC July 1515; They had 1 son (Henry) and 2 daughters (Katherine, wife of Sir Francis Hastings, 2nd Earl of Huntingdon; & Winifred, wife of Sir Thomas Hastings, & of Sir Thomas Barrington).3,4,5,6,7,8,9 Jane Neville died between 4 Jun
2 CONC e 1535 and 26 October 1538.3,6,9
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir Henry Pole, Lord Montague, High Steward of Tewkesbury Abbey & of Hornby Abbey b. Jun 1492, d. 9 Jan 1539
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Katherine Pole+12,3,5,6,8,9 b. c 1516, d. 23 Sep 1576
2 CONT **Winifred Pole13,3,6,9 b. a 1521, d. 22 Feb 1602
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S8471] Unknown author, The Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles, by Gerald Paget, Vol. 2, p. 247; Plantagenet Ancestry of 17th Century Colonists, by David Faris, p. 255.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 95.
2 CONT * 3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 587.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 171.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 374-375.
2 CONT * 6.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 377.
2 CONT * 7.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 325.
2 CONT * 8.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. III, p. 371.
2 CONT * 9.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 399-400.
2 CONT * 10.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 170.
2 CONT * 11.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 323-324.
2 CONT * 12.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 387.
2 CONT * 13.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. IX, p. 96, notes.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p911.htm#i27360 _______________________
2 CONT *'''Henry Pole, 1st Baron Montagu (also written Montague or Montacute'''; born circa 1492 – died 9 January 1539), the only holder of the title Baron Montagu under its 1514 creation, was one of the relatives King Henry VIII of Engl
2 CONC and had executed for treason.
2 CONT *Henry Pole was the oldest son of Margaret Pole, 8th Countess of Salisbury, and Sir Richard Pole. He was invested as a knight by King Henry VIII in 1513 and summoned to Parliament as Baron Montagu in the Peerage of England on 12 O
2 CONC ctober 1514. He was appointed steward of manors belonging to the Tewkesbury Abbey in 1526. From 1530 on he became justice of the peace for Somerset, Dorset, Hampshire and Sussex.[1][2]
2 CONT *'''In May 1510 or before May 1520, Pole married Jane Neville, daughter of George Nevill, 5th Baron Bergavenny, and Joan Arundel. They had the following children:
2 CONT ** Catherine Pole (1511 - 23 September 1576) married Francis Hastings, 2nd Earl of Huntingdon.
2 CONT ** Lucy Pole, married Anthony Browne.
2 CONT ** Thomas Pole (d. 1526), married Elizabeth Wingfield. Without issue.
2 CONT ** Henry Pole (aft. 1520 or in 1521 – aft. September 1542), married Margaret Neville. According to Alison Weir he was born in 1527. He was imprisoned from an early age at the Tower of London until his death.[3]
2 CONT ** Winifred Pole (b. aft. 1521 or in 1525), married firstly Sir Thomas Hastings (1515–1558, buried Stoke Poges, Buckinghamshire, the brother of her sister Catherine's husband), son of George Hastings, 1st Earl of Huntingdon, witho
2 CONC ut issue, and secondly, Sir Thomas Barrington of Barrington Hall, Hatfield Broadoak, Essex (died 1586). By the second Sir Thomas, Winifred had the following children: Catherine Barrington, married in 1584 to William Bourchier, gre
2 CONC at-grandson of John Bourchier, 2nd Baron Berners (a son of Catherine and William was Sir John Bourchier a regicide of King Charles I of England); Sir Francis Barrington, 1st Baronet; John Barrington.
2 CONT *'''On 4 November 1538, Montagu along with his wife,[4] his wife's brother Edward Neville and other relatives were arrested on a charge of treason by King Henry VIII''', though Thomas Cromwell had previously written that they had 
2 CONC "little offended save that he is of their kin." Montagu's brother Reginald was not among them, in exile at the time, due to his opposition of King Henry's divorce from Catherine of Aragon. '''They were committed to the Tower of Lo
2 CONC ndon and Lord Montagu was attainted and his honours forfeited on 2 December 1538. On 9 January 1539, with the exception of Sir Geoffrey Pole, Henry's brother, all the arrestees were beheaded.''' (Neville had been beheaded earlier 
2 CONC on 8 December 1538). Henry Courtenay, 1st Marquess of Exeter, was arrested along with his wife and 11-year old son ....
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Pole,_11th_Baron_Montacute ________________________
2 CONT *JANE NEVILLE WIFE OF SIR HENRY POLE IS LISTED IN OTHER REFERENCES AS THE DAU. OF SIR GEORGE NEVILLE & JOAN FITZALAN, GRANDDAUGHTER OF MARGARET (FENNE) & SIR GEORGE 2ND LORD
2 CONT *'''Jane Neville [1]
2 CONT *'''F, #107584, d. before 26 October 1538
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 Jan 2011
2 CONT *'''Jane Neville was the daughter of Sir George Neville, 2nd Lord Abergavenny and Margaret Fenne.1,2 She married Sir Henry Pole, 1st Lord Montagu, son of Sir Richard Pole and Margaret Plantagenet, Countess of Salisbury, before May
2 CONC  1520.3 She died before 26 October 1538.2
2 CONT *'''      From before May 1520, her married name became Pole.3
2 CONT *'''Children of Jane Neville and Sir Henry Pole, 1st Lord Montagu
2 CONT ** 1.Catherine Pole+3 b. a 1520, d. 23 Sep 1576
2 CONT ** 2.Henry Pole3 b. a 1520, d. a Sep 1542
2 CONT ** 3.Winifred Pole+3 b. a 1521
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 136. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT * 2.[S8] Volume 1, page 18. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S8]
2 CONT * 3.[S8] See. [S8]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p10759.htm#i107584 _______________________
2 CONT *JANE NEVILLE WIFE OF SIR HENRY POLE IS LISTED IN OTHER REFERENCES AS THE DAU. OF SIR GEORGE NEVILLE & JOAN FITZALAN, GRANDDAUGHTER OF MARGARET (FENNE) & SIR GEORGE 2ND LORD
2 CONT *'''Jane NEVILLE
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1481, Abergavenny, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT *'''Died: 9 Jan 1538/39
2 CONT *Father: George NEVILLE (2° B. Abergavenny)
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret FENNE
2 CONT *'''Married: Henry POLE (B. Montagu) May 1510, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Catherine POLE (C. Huntingdon)
2 CONT **2. Thomas POLE
2 CONT **3. Henry POLE
2 CONT **3. Winifred POLE
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/NEVILLE4.htm#Jane NEVILLE1  _________________________
