2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Stafford, 1st Baron Stafford (18 September 1501 - 30 April 1563) was born in Penshurst, Kent, England the eldest son and second child of Edward Stafford, 3rd Duke of Buckingham and Alianore Percy, Duchess of Buckingham. Alia
2 CONC nore was the daughter of Henry Percy, 4th Earl of Northumberland and Maud Herbert, Countess of Northumberland. He was created Baron Stafford in 1547.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married Ursula Pole, Baroness Stafford the daughter of Margaret Pole, 8th Countess of Salisbury and Sir Richard Pole. Margaret was a daughter of George Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Clarence  and Isabella Neville. Henry and Ursul
2 CONC a had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Henry Stafford, 2nd Baron Stafford (bef 1534 -1 January 1565) who married Elizabeth Davy before 25 September 1557.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Edward Stafford, 3rd Baron Stafford 17 January 1535 -18 October 1603). He was buried on 21 October 1603 at St. Mary's Church, Stafford. He had married Maria Stanley, Baroness Stafford, daughter of Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of De
2 CONC rby and Dorothy Howard, Countess of Derby. Dorothy was daughter of Thomas Howard, 2nd Duke of Norfolk  and Agnes Tilney.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were parents to:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Edward Stafford (b. 27 January 1568) buried on the 1 February 1568 at St. Mary's Church, Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Edward Stafford, 4th Baron Stafford (1572 -1625) who married Isabel Forster in about 1595:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Henry Stafford, 5th Baron Stafford (1621 -1637).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Mary Stafford, 1st Countess Stafford (1619 -1693) who married William Howard, 1st Viscount Stafford in 1637; they had children. {Viscount Howard was also known as Baron Stafford).
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Dorothy Stafford (b. about 1572).
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Richard Stafford who married Mary Corbet, daughter of John Corbet and Anne Booth .
2 CONT
2 CONT They were parents to:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Roger Stafford (Floyde), 6th Baron Stafford (about 1572 -1640) who died very poor.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Jane Stafford (about 1581 after 1637.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Thomas Stafford (1531 - 4 May 1557) who was captured and executed for High Treason in Scarborough.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Walter Stafford (about 1539 -after 1571).
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. William Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Elizabeth Stafford who married Sir William Neville (b. about 1524).
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Dorothy Stafford (about 1526 -23 September 1603) who married Sir William Stafford of Grafton after July 1543.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were parents to:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sir Edward Stafford of Grafton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Sir John Stafford of Marlwood Park.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. William Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Elizabeth Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Anne Stafford who married Sir Henry Williams (1516 - 1551). Sir Henry was buried on the 20 August 1551 in London
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Stafford, 1st Baron Stafford (18 September 1501-30 April 1563) was born in Penshurst, Kent, England the eldest son and second child of Edward Stafford, 3rd Duke of Buckingham and Eleanor Percy, Duchess of Buckingham. Eleanor
2 CONC  (or Alianore) was the daughter of Henry Percy, 4th Earl of Northumberland and Maud Herbert, Countess of Northumberland. He was created Baron Stafford in 1547.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married Ursula Pole, Baroness Stafford the daughter of Margaret Pole, 8th Countess of Salisbury and Sir Richard Pole. Margaret was a daughter of George Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Clarence and Isabella Neville. Henry and Ursula
2 CONC  had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry Stafford, 2nd Baron Stafford (bef 1534-1 January 1565) who married Elizabeth Davy before 25 September 1557.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Edward Stafford, 3rd Baron Stafford (17 January 1535-18 October 1603). He was buried on 21 October 1603 at St. Mary's Church, Stafford. He had married Maria Stanley, Baroness Stafford, daughter of Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of
2 CONC  Derby and Dorothy Howard, Countess of Derby. Dorothy was daughter of Thomas Howard, 2nd Duke of Norfolk and Agnes Tilney. They were parents to:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Edward Stafford (b. 27 January 1568) buried on the 1 February 1568 at St. Mary's Church, Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Edward Stafford, 4th Baron Stafford (1572-1625) who married Isabel Forster in about 1595:
2 CONT
2 CONT                 + Henry Stafford, 5th Baron Stafford (1621-1637).
2 CONT
2 CONT                 + Mary Stafford, 1st Countess Stafford (1619-1693) who married William Howard, 1st Viscount Stafford in 1637; they had children. {Viscount Howard was also known as Baron Stafford}.
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Dorothy Stafford (b. about 1572).
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Richard Stafford who married Mary Corbet, daughter of John Corbet and Anne Booth . They were parents to:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Roger Stafford (Floyde), 6th Baron Stafford (about 1572-1640) who died very poor.
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Jane Stafford (about 1581-after 1637), married Sir Thomas Beaumont.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Thomas Stafford (1531-4 May 1557) who was captured and executed for High Treason in Scarborough.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Walter Stafford (about 1539-after 1571).
2 CONT
2 CONT     * William Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Elizabeth Stafford who married Sir William Neville (b. about 1524).
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Dorothy Stafford (about 1526-23 September 1603) who married Sir William Stafford of Rochford after July 1543. They were parents to:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Ursula Stafford (about 1553). Her husband Richard Drake became Equerry to Queen Elizabeth in 1577.
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Sir Edward Stafford of Grafton.
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Sir John Stafford of Marlwood Park.)
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Elizabeth Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anne Stafford who married Sir Henry Williams (1516-1551). Sir Henry was buried on the 20 August 1551 in London.
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________________________
