1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry Radclyffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex, KG (also spelled "Radcliffe") (1507 – 17 February 1557) was a son of Robert Radclyffe, 1st Earl of Sussex and his wife Elizabeth Stafford, Countess of Sussex.
2 CONT
2 CONT His maternal grandparents were Henry Stafford, 2nd Duke of Buckingham and his wife Catherine Woodville.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a second cousin to among others Thomas Grey, 2nd Marquess of Dorset, Arthur, Prince of Wales, Margaret, queen consort of Scotland, Henry VIII of England, Elizabeth Tudor, Mary, queen consort of France, Edmund Tudor, Duke of
2 CONC  Somerset, Katherine Tudor, Henry Courtenay, 1st Marquess of Exeter, Margaret Courtenay and Henry Somerset, 2nd Earl of Worcester.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was first married to Elizabeth Howard, a daughter of Thomas Howard, 2nd Duke of Norfolk and his second wife Agnes Tilney. They had two sons:
2 CONT * Thomas Radclyffe, 3rd Earl of Sussex (c. 1525 – 9 June 1583).
2 CONT * Henry Radclyffe, 4th Earl of Sussex (c. 1532–1593).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Complete Peerage gives the date of death for his first wife as 18 September 1534. Burke's Peerage agrees on the date but changes the year to 1537. Either way Henry would not remain a widower for long.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married secondly Anne Calthorpe. The marriage resulted in a divorce or annulment in 1555. But they had two known children:
2 CONT * Egremont Radclyffe (died 1578). He took part in the Rising of the North but escaped to Continental Europe after its failure. He was executed in Namur, accused of attempting to poison John of Austria. John is believed to have die
2 CONC d of typhus.
2 CONT * Lady Frances Radclyffe (died 1602). Married Sir Thomas Mildmay, by whom she had two sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 27 November 1542 his father died and Henry succeeded him as Earl of Sussex. His second cousin Mary I created him a Knight of the Garter in 1554, alongside the later Philip II of Spain, Emmanuel Philibert, Duke of Savoy and Will
2 CONC iam Howard, 1st Baron Howard of Effingham.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Radclyffe,_2nd_Earl_of_Sussex ________________
2 CONT *'''Sir Henry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex, Viscount FitzWalter1
2 CONT *'''M, #48568, b. circa 1507, d. 17 February 1557
2 CONT *Father      Sir Robert Radcliffe, 1st Earl Sussex, Viscount FitzWalter, 7th Lord FitzWalter, Great Chamberlain of England2 b. c 1483, d. 27 Nov 1542
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth Stafford2 d. bt 1 Jan 1530 - 11 May 1532
2 CONT *'''     Sir Henry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex, Viscount FitzWalter was born circa 1507.1 He married Elizabeth Howard, daughter of Sir Thomas Howard, Earl Marshal of England, 2nd Duke Norfolk, Sheriff of Norfolk & Suffolk, Lord 
2 CONC High Treasurer and Agnes Tilney, before 21 May 1524.1,3 Sir Henry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex, Viscount FitzWalter married Anne Calthorpe, daughter of Sir Philip Calthorpe and Jane Blennerhassett, before 21 November 1538.4 Sir H
2 CONC enry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex, Viscount FitzWalter and Anne Calthorpe were divorced on 13 November 1555 at London, Middlesex, England; By Act of Parliament.4 Sir Henry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex, Viscount FitzWalter died o
2 CONC n 17 February 1557 at Home of Sir Henry Sydney, London, Middlesex, England.1
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Elizabeth Howard b. c 1499, d. 18 Sep 1534
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Anne Calthorpe d. bt 22 Aug 1579 - 28 Mar 1582
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. XII/1, p. 520-522. 
2 CONT *2.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. XII/1, p. 520.
2 CONT * 3.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 236-237.
2 CONT * 4.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. XII/1, p. 521.
