2 CONT *'''Henry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex1
2 CONT *'''M, #160113, b. circa 1506, d. 17 February 1556/57
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Sep 2013
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.04%
2 CONT *'''     Henry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex was born circa 1506 at Knock-Aloe-Moar, Patrick, Isle of Man.1 He was the son of Robert Radcliffe, 1st Earl of Sussex and Lady Elizabeth Stafford.1,2 He married, firstly, Lady Elizabeth
2 CONC  Howard, daughter of Thomas Howard, 2nd Duke of Norfolk and Agnes Tilney, before 21 May 1524.3 He married, secondly, Anne Calthorp, daughter of Sir Philip Calthorp, before 21 November 1538.4 He and Anne Calthorp were divorced befo
2 CONC re 13 November 1555.4 He died on 17 February 1556/57.4
2 CONT *'''      In 1527 in the suite of Wolsey on the latter's Embassy to France.4 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Bath (K.B.) in 1533.4 He succeeded to the title of 2nd Viscount FitzWalter [E., 1525] on 27 November 1542.4 He 
2 CONC succeeded to the title of 11th Lord FitzWalter [E., 1295] on 27 November 1542.4 He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Sussex [E., 1529] on 27 November 1542.4 In 1544 he campaigned in France.4 He held the office of Joint Lord-Li
2 CONC eutenant of Norfolk between 1551 and 1553.4 He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) in 1553.4 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) in 1554.4 He held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of Norfolk and Suffolk betw
2 CONC een February 1556 and 1556/57.4
2 CONT *'''Children of Henry Radcliffe, 2nd Earl of Sussex and Anne Calthorp
