2 CONT Please see Peter Bartrum: Perrot 2; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173426969987 (Steven Ferry, August 8, 2024.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~parrott/genealogy/pembrokeshire.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Owain (Owen) Perrot (d 1521) of Haroldston. Married Catherine Poyntz, daughter of Sir Robert Poyntz of Iron Acton, Gloucestershire, whose mother was a daughter of Anthony Wydeville, Baron Scales (1460) and the Earl of Rivers a
2 CONC nd Scales (1569). He was brother in law to Edward IV.  Knighted 1513.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Oldest son Robert, heir, died young (d 1522) & with no issue. As his father died while Robert was a minor, Robert was placed in the custody of 2 knights.
2 CONT # Son Thomas, see #13 below
2 CONT # Daughter Mary, first wife of Gryffyth (Gruffudd) White
2 CONT # White, of Henllan, Rhoscrowdder, Pembrokeshire, Wales
2 CONT # Daughter Elizabeth (Elsbeth, b 1517), married ~1538 to Thomas Audley (b ~1513) of St. Ives, Cornwall, England (not listed by Turvey)
2 CONT # Richard of Brook near Claymore - had illegitimate son, Richard
2 CONT # 4th son, John Perrot (d ~1560s) started the family branch in Carmarthen,
2 CONT # Rys (Rice/Richard) Perrott (d. 1571), who lived in Sandwitch, Kent. Tutored King Edward VI in Greek. Became a bailiff of Sandwich in 1557, its M.P. in 1563, then its mayor 1565-66. He was also bailiff and verger for Sir Thomas C
2 CONC heyney.
2 CONT # A son Edward is sometimes listed
