1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Aimée Motier de La Fayette (c. 1480 – 1556) was a prominent 16th-century French noblewoman and courtier. She is best remembered as a trusted companion to Marguerite de Navarre (sister of King Francis I) and as the governess and Da
2 CONC me d'Honneur to Jeanne d'Albret, the Queen of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her life and historical footprint can be summarized by a few key details:
2 CONT
2 CONT Court Position: She was known at the French court as "la Baillive de Caen," a title derived from her marriage to François de Silly, who held the position of bailli (bailiff) of Caen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Loyalty to the Crown: She famously remained by the side of Marguerite de Navarre during the tense captivity of King Francis I in Madrid after the Battle of Pavia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal Rewards: To thank her for her fierce loyalty, King Francis I granted her the barony of l'Aigle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal Governess: She served as the governess for Jeanne d'Albret—the daughter of Marguerite de Navarre. Jeanne d'Albret would eventually become the mother of King Henry IV of France. Aimée passed away at Pau's Castle in 1556.
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Portraits: She is recognized in art history for her iconic portraits. Notable depictions painted by celebrated Renaissance artists like Jean Clouet and Corneille de Lyon reside in collections such as the Ashmolean Museu
2 CONC m and the Musée Condé.
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT https://www.album-online.com/detail/en/ZGJlNTJlMA/aimee-motier-fayette-c16th-century-1939-c-1480-1539-portrait-alb3924394 
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Motier-25 
2 CONT https://www.nationalgalleries.org/art-and-artists/254167 
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/castel974?lang=en&n=motier+de+la+fayette&p=aimee&type=tree 
2 CONT https://man8rove.com/fr/profile/qn9883f-aimee-motier-de-la-fayette 
2 CONT https://www.heritage-images.com/preview/aimee-motier-de-la-fayette-c16th-century-1939-artist-corneille-de-lyon-2649992
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT For a quick look at her famous descendant, the Marquis de Lafayette, who helped shape the American Revolution: https://www.youtube.com/shorts/VHHpMSe8LnY 
