1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The survival of the Maignelay title depended not on a direct heir, but on a strategic transfer to the sword-arm of the Maintenay branch.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Gen 17) Florimond d'Halluin; Marquis de Maignelay, Governor of La Fère
2 CONT The Northern Gatekeeper
2 CONT I. Profile Data (FL)
2 CONT Full Name: Florimond d'Halluin
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation: 17
2 CONT Status: Lineage Successor; Head of the Maignelay branch
2 CONT Strategic Role: Family Protector; responsible for securing and carrying forward the Maignelay peerage
2 CONT Titles: Marquis de Maignelay, Governor of La Fère
2 CONT Filiation: Third son of Jean d'Halluin and Marguerite de Montmorency
2 CONT Active Period (Flourished): c. 1600–1630
2 CONT
2 CONT '''II. Biographical Sketch: The Historical Context'''
2 CONT Florimond d'Halluin emerged as a central figure during the early 17th-century consolidation of the French state under the Bourbon monarchy. As a younger son of a high-noble house, his career was defined by military utility and adm
2 CONC inistrative service to the Crown rather than primary inheritance.
2 CONT
2 CONT His tenure as Governor of La Fère (c. 1611) placed him in command of a critical fortress on the Oise River, serving as a primary defensive buffer against the Spanish Netherlands. During this period, when the senior Halluin-Piennes
2 CONC  line faced a successional crisis, Florimond became the primary beneficiary of a Branch Transfer. By formally securing the Marquisat de Maignelay in 1612, he ensured that the prestige of the Piennes branch was preserved through th
2 CONC e rising Maintenay line.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''III. Heraldry'''
2 CONT Blazon: Argent, three lions rampant sable, armed, langued, and crowned or.
2 CONT
2 CONT Quartering: Florimond's achievement typically quartered the Halluin lions with the Montmorency alerions (Or, a cross gules cantoned with sixteen alerions azure).
2 CONT
2 CONT Heraldic Significance: The inclusion of the alerions acts as a visual document of the high-value Montmorency alliance that defined his branch's social standing.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''IV. Forensic Correction Log'''
2 CONT '''Finding: Identification of the "Maignelay Transfer"'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Traditional Claim: Often cited as a standard inheritance from senior relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Correction: Identified specifically as a Branch-to-Branch Transfer from the Piennes line to the Maintenay line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rationale: Curator Logic and the User Correction Ledger dictate this was a strategic acquisition to rescue a failing title rather than standard primogeniture.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Finding: Administrative Separation'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Traditional Claim: Conflation of various Halluin governors in older genealogical narratives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Correction: Florimond’s service is isolated strictly to the Governorship of La Fère.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rationale: Applying the Cawley Standard of primary source primacy, royal commissions identify Florimond specifically for this frontier post.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''V. Documentation and Evidence (The Auditor’s Trail)'''
2 CONT * Primary Administrative Record: 1612 Letters Patent (Parliament of Paris) confirming the registration and transfer of the Marquisat de Maignelay.
2 CONT * Military Commission: 1611 Records of the Secrétariat d'État à la Guerre documenting the commission for the Governor of La Fère.
2 CONT * Charles Cawley (MedLands Methodology): Filiation verified by applying the Cawley Standard, requiring contemporary proof of parentage to pass the Biological Clock test.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''VI. User Correction Ledger:''' 
2 CONT Explicit override of traditional lists that fail to distinguish the Maintenay branch's administrative service from the senior ducal branch.
2 CONT
2 CONT <span style="color:red; font-weight:bold;">DISCLAIMER: This profile is drafted as a Forensic Audit with AI assistance. It prioritizes the "Paper Trail" of the French Royal Household and the Cawley/Warlop standards of evidence over
2 CONC  traditional narratives. (This summary is intended for research leads only; cross-verification with original primary documentation is essential for final lineage certification.)</span>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Rest of the Story:'''
2 CONT '''The Fine Print of French Peerage Law'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 16th-century France, when a King elevated an estate into a Duchy-Peerage (Duché-Pairie), the title was not fully active the moment the King signed the paper. To become an official Pair de France, the recipient had to take those
2 CONC  royal Letters Patent to the Parlement of Paris to be formally registered (enregistré).
2 CONT * '''1. Charles (The 1st Duke)'''
2 CONT He received the ducal elevation from King Henri III in 1587.
2 CONT He successfully registered it with the Parlement of Paris. He was, without question, the 1st Duke.
2 CONT * '''2. Florimond (The 2nd Duke — The Non-Registered Holder)'''
2 CONT When Charles died, Florimond assumed the title of Duc d'Halluin by blood right.
2 CONT '''The Catch:''' Florimond operated at the absolute height of the chaotic French Wars of Religion. He was busy serving as Governor of La Fère and fighting on the front lines. Because of the war, he never had the opportunity to tra
2 CONC vel to Paris to register his succession with the Parlement.
2 CONT Because he was assassinated before he could complete this bureaucratic step, later official parliamentary registries sometimes skipped his name in the formal ledger of peers, tracking him simply as Marquis de Maignelay. However, i
2 CONC n contemporary military commissions and family deeds, he used and held the title of Duke.
2 CONT * '''3. Anne (The 2nd Official Duchess)'''
2 CONT Because Florimond died without male heirs, his daughter Anne d'Halluin inherited the entire family fortune.
2 CONT When she married Charles de Schomberg, the French crown issued new Letters Patent confirming her as the hereditary Duchesse d'Halluin.
2 CONT And because she and her husband successfully registered these papers with the Parlement, she appears in the official historical peerage lists as the 2nd confirmed holder of the active title.
