1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Gray-of-Harwich/6000000030692051040?through=6000000146360241824#/tab/media
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Thomas Grey was born in 1526.2 He was the son of Thomas Grey, 2nd Marquess of Dorset and Margaret Wotton.1,2 He died after 1554, executed for participating in Wyatt's rebellion.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lord Thomas Grey
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Grey+1 Married: John (Astley) ASHLEY (Sir) ABT 1581
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Do not confuse  Thomas Gray of Harwich, the father of John Gray and grandfather of Thomas Gray, with Lord Thomas Grey the son of the 2nd Marquess of Dorset who was executed for treason in 1555. Lord Thomas was of an entirely diffe
2 CONC rent social class, being the uncle of Lady Jane Grey, who was Queen of England for nine days, and he certainly was not the father of John Gray of Harwich. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1554  Lord John Grey and Lord Thomas Grey,  & Suffolk took part in Wyatt's rebellion against Mary I's marriage to Philip of Spain and in support of Lady Jane Grey.[29] 
2 CONT
2 CONT When this rebellion failed, all three were arrested, and Suffolk and his brother Thomas were executed,[29] as were Lady Jane herself and her husband Lord Guilford Dudley.[28]
2 CONT
2 CONT Gray family and Wyatts and Wyatts Rebellion: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Encyclopedia of Tudor England, Volume 1.  By John A. Wagner, Susan Walters Schmid.  Page 529. [https://books.google.com/books?id=EUCY3otvttEC&pg=PA529&lpg=PA529&dq=wyatts+rebellion+thomas+grey&source=bl&ots=dfWwyh3T_t&sig=KQyEfn_Y
2 CONC Z0FTCYutIU48qcDiYr0&hl=en&sa=X&ei=iMuqVIj2MIWgyQSv84KgAw&ved=0CDEQ6AEwCA#v=onepage&q=wyatts%20rebellion%20thomas%20grey&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________
2 CONT
