1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Sutton&GSiman=1&GScid=638911&GRid=119796199& Sir Edward Sutton] Find A Grave Memorial# 119796199
2 CONT * Source: http://atropesend.blogspot.com/2010/05/anges-henry-viii-anne-boleyn-and.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Sutton, 4th Baron Dudley
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Sutton, 4th Baron Dudley (1525 - 12 July 1586) was the son of John Sutton, 3rd Baron Dudley and Lady Cicely Grey, and the grandson of Edmund Sutton, Knight of Dudley castle and Baron Tibertot and Cherleton (born 1425).
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward succeeded his father as Baron Dudley in 1553, and at one time is thought to have been a Governor of Hume castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward married:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1). Katherine Brydges, the daughter of Sir John Brydges the 1st Baron Chandos of Sudeley and Elizabeth (nee Grey) of Wilton (m. 1556)
2 CONT
2 CONT (2). (m. 1567) Jane Stanley, (a daughter of Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of Derby). By the Lady Jane Stanley he had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i) Edward Dudley, who became the 5th Baron Dudley - (b. 17 September 1567, d. 23 June 1643).
2 CONT
2 CONT ii) John Dudley - (b. 30 November 1569, d. c. Feb 1644/45).
2 CONT
2 CONT (3). (m. 1570) Mary, the daughter of William, 1st Baron Howard.
2 CONT
2 CONT This branch of the Dudley family is of great interest to many family historians, especially in the United States where his cousins seem to have settled.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is buried at St. Margaret's Church, Westminster, London, England. He was succeeded by his son, Edward Sutton, 5th Baron Dudley (1556-1643).
