2 CONC ward was at that time in the Tower, facing execution, and the King was known to be looking for a sixth bride. '''Lucy was the daughter''' of Henry Somerset, 2nd E. of Worcester and Lord Herbert of Ragland. '''She may have been sty
2 CONC led Lady Lucy Herbert and Chapuys’s 'Albart' would be typical of his misspellings of English names. Lucy’s mother''' was Elizabeth Browne, the sister of Sir Anthony Browne, thus explaining Chapuys’s further identification of her a
2 CONC s Browne’s niece. '''Lucy was a maid of honor to Catherine Howard and in 1545 married Queen Catherine Parr’s stepson, John Neville, 4th baron Latimer, and was part of Catherine’s household as Lady Latimer.
