1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Family and Education b. by 1532, 3rd s. of Henry Somerset, 2nd Earl of Worcester by 2nd w. Elizabeth, da. of Sir Anthony Browne; bro. of Charles† and Thomas. unm. 1s. 1da. illegit.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices Held
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography On 3 Jan. 1553 Francis Somerset obtained a pardon for burglary and other crimes and the restoration of the lands that he had forfeited in punishment. He was to make his name as a soldier and his Membership was an interlu
2 CONC de in his career. His return to Mary’s last Parliament was disputed by William Herbert IV who claimed that he and William Morgan had been re-elected. The attorney-general acted upon the information laid by Herbert, but the sheriff
2 CONC  Henry Lewis failed to appear before the Exchequer to answer the allegation until Trinity term 1559. Because no jury travelled up with Lewis the case went on nisi prius to the Monmouthshire assizes, where the validity of Somerset’
2 CONC s election was upheld, but since this verdict was not reached until eight months after the dissolution it merely confirmed the right to sit which he had probably exercised. In 1557 Somerset had served in France as a captain under 
2 CONC his brother the 3rd Earl of Worcester and during the prorogation a year later he conducted 300 men from Guisnes to the Scottish border where his action in the field earned him Mary’s thanks. His command was renewed by Elizabeth an
2 CONC d it was during an attack upon Le Havre that he died on 22 July 1563. He had made his will two months earlier dividing most of his possessions between his brothers Charles and Thomas. He left his black armour to his cousin the 13t
2 CONC h Lord Grey of Wilton and his portrait to his mistress. Thomas Somerset proved the will on 5 Jan. 1564.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref Volumes: 1509-1558 Author: P. S. Edwards Notes 1. Date of birth estimated from first reference. Bradney, Mon. ii(1), 26; PCC 3 Stevenson. 2. CPR, 1550-3, p. 402; E159/338, Easter 48; HMC Foljambe, 6; APC, vi. 337, 396; CSP Sco
2 CONC t. 1547-63, nos. 487, 759, 778, 839, 848; CSP For. 1558-9, nos. 527, 974; 1559-60, nos. 276 (2, 3), 327(1), 1088; 1560-3, nos. 421 (1, 2), 471(9), 476, 484(4), 537(3), 599, 966, 1563, nos. 226, 282, 289, 391(4), 664, 896(1), 1045(
2 CONC 2); CSP Dom. 1601-3, Add. 1547-65, p. 481; PCC 3 Stevenson.
