1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Mary SOMERSET
2 CONT *'''Died: AFT 1578
2 CONT *Father: Henry SOMERSET (2º E. Worcester)
2 CONT *Mother: Elizabeth BROWNE (C. Worcester)
2 CONT *'''Married: Edward DALE
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/SOMERSET.htm#Mary SOMERSET1 _______________
2 CONT
2 CONT There are a lot of questions about her, including whether she was the same "Mary Somerset" who married Edward Dale (who appears to have been https://www.geni.com/people/Rev-Edward-Dale/6000000027935783295 of Alford, Lincolnshire).
2 CONC  An Earl's legitimate daughter could be expected to make a far more brilliant marriage than an obscure country parson.
2 CONT
2 CONT It needs to be noted that ''anyone'' with ancestors from Somersetshire might take the surname "Somerset".
2 CONT
2 CONT The account in "A Who's Who of Tudor Women" is not trustworthy, because https://www.geni.com/people/Governor-Sir-Thomas-Dale/6000000001795734098 ''must'' have been born by 1575 at the very latest in order for him to have been as a
2 CONC ctive in the Low Countries for as long as he was. Therefore he cannot possibly have been Rev. Edward Dale's '''grand'''son. (It is of course quite possible that he wasn't related at all and the whole thing was just one of those hi
2 CONC storical fables.)
