1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Somerset, 3rd Earl of Worcester, KG''' (c. 1526  – 21 February 1589) was born before 1526 to Henry Somerset, 2nd Earl of Worcester and his second wife Elizabeth Browne. [first wife Margaret Courtenay, according to the D
2 CONC NB; died before 15 April 1526. Some sources say the union produced no children.]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 26 November 1549, he succeeded his father and became the 3rd Earl of Worcester.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12em>{{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000225578467964&size=large|200px|Quartered arms of Sir William Somerset, 3rd Earl of Worcester}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Worcester supported Lady Jane Grey in 1553. He was invested as Knight Companion of the Order of the Garter (KG) in 1570. He was a patron of the arts, and sponsored - among others - the Elizabethan actor Edward Alleyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT In January 1573, he was sent to France to the baptism of Marie Elisabeth of France. His ship was attacked by pirates, who captured a second boat carrying several of his attendants.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Before 19 May 1550, Worcester married Christiana North, daughter of Edward North, 1st Baron North and his wife Alice Squire.[3] They were parents to three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Edward Somerset, 4th Earl of Worcester (d. 3 March 1628).
2 CONT # Elizabeth Somerset. Married William Windsor. He was a namesake son of William Windsor, 2nd Baron Windsor by his wife Margaret Sambourne.
2 CONT # Lucy Somerset. Married Henry Herbert, Esquire.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Somerset re-married (2nd) before 1567 Theophila Newton, daughter of John Newton (otherwise Cradock), Knt., of East Harptree, Somerset, by Margaret, daughter of Anthony Poyntz, Knt. A portrait of Countess Theophila by an un
2 CONC known artist of that date is mentioned by Ashelford, Visual History of Costume (1983): 72. Theophila survived him and is said to have married (2) William Paratt, of Pantglas.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Somerset also had three illegitimate daughters:[1]
2 CONT * Anne, married William Probert, Esq.
2 CONT * Mary, married William Hughes, Esq.
2 CONT * ___
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William died "at his house at Hackney 21 Feb. 1588/9, and was buried at Raglan Monmoughshire. He left a will proved 7 Nov. 1589."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
