2 DATE ABT 1521
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1549
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edmund Sheffield, 1st Baron Sheffield, of Butterwick [disambiguation needed] (22 November 1521 – 19 July 1549) was an English nobleman, the son of Sir Robert Sheffield (died 15 November 1531, son of Robert Sheffiel
2 CONC d and Helen Delves) and his second wife Jane Stanley, daughter of George Stanley, 9th Baron Strange and Joan le Strange, 9th Baroness Strange. Through his mother, he was a second cousin of the reigning English monarch, King Henry 
2 CONC VIII.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT Following his father's death in 1531, his wardship was granted to George Boleyn, Viscount Rochford, the brother of Henry VIII's second wife, Anne Boleyn. However, both Rochford and Boleyn were executed in 1536, and his wardship wa
2 CONC s transferred to John de Vere, the fifteenth Earl of Oxford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund married Lady Anne de Vere, Oxford's daughter, before 31 January 1538, and had five children. In 1547 he was raised to the Peerage of England as Baron Sheffield of Butterwick. Two years later, during Kett's Rebellion in Norw
2 CONC ich, Lord Sheffield was killed in a street near the Cathedral Close when he fell from his horse and was struck by a butcher.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT * 1.Eleanor Sheffield (born about 1537) married Denzel Holles
2 CONT * 2.John Sheffield, 2nd Baron Sheffield (c. 1538 – 10 December 1568) married Douglas Howard
2 CONT * 3.Robert Sheffield (born about 1540
2 CONT * 4.Frances Sheffield (born 1542) married Thomas Metham
2 CONT * 5.Elizabeth Sheffield (born about 1546)
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT *1.^ Strype, John, Ecclesiastical Memoirs, vol.2 part 1, Oxford (1822), 272.
2 CONT ** Summerson, Henry, "Sheffield, Edmund", on the website of the Oxford Dictionary of National Biography (subscription or UK public library membership required)
