2 CONT
2 CONT ANNE HASTINGS (c.1485-November 17, 1550)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Hastings was the daughter of Edward, 2nd baron Hastings (November 25, 1466-November 8, 1506) and Mary Hungerford (c.1468-July 10, 1533). Anne was married to John Radcliffe, Lord Fitzwalter (1442-1496) as a child. In 1507, she
2 CONC  married Thomas Stanley, 2nd earl of Derby (1485-May 23, 1521) and was the mother of Edward, 3rd earl (May 10,1508-October 24,1572), John, Anne, Margaret (d. January 1534), Henry (d. June 29, 1528), James, George, Thomas (c.1515-1
2 CONC 538), and Jane. Anne was at the court of Catherine of Aragon as the youngest of her ladies in waiting in 1509 and at the Field of Cloth of Gold in 1520. In 1542, when her son-in-law, Robert, earl of Sussex, died he gave Anne custo
2 CONC dy of his daughter, Jane (her mother was Anne's late daughter Margaret) as well as the wardship of young Lord Berkeley, intended as the girl's husband. In 1545, Anne sold Berkeley's wardship to his mother for £1000. In her will, A
2 CONC nne left Jane clothing, furnishings, and the profits of that sale.
2 CONT
2 CONT src: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/Stanley1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st wife - Catherine Howard, m. 1529
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd wife - Dorothy Howard m. 21 feb 1530
2 CONT    children: Henry, Mary, Thomas, Jane, Anne, Catherine
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd wife - unknown
2 CONT    children: Elizabeth, Margaret, Edward
2 CONT
2 CONT 4th wife - Margaret Barlow  m. 1547, d. 19 jan 1558
2 CONT
2 CONT 5th wife - Marry Cotton m. bef Jan 1561/62. d. 16 nov 1580. she married 2nd Henry Grey, 6th earl of Kent.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/LH1M-6J7
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of Derby
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 10 May 1509, d. 24 October 1572
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of Derby was born on 10 May 1509. He was the son of Thomas Stanley, 2nd Earl of Derby and Anne Hastings.He married, secondly, Margaret Barlow, daughter of Ellis Barlow.He married, firstly, Lady Dorothy How
2 CONC ard, daughter of Thomas Howard, 2nd Duke of Norfolk and Agnes Tilney, circa 21 February 1530.He married, thirdly, Mary Cotton, daughter of Rt. Hon. Sir George Cotton, before 1 January 1561/62. He died on 24 October 1572 at age 63.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of Derby succeeded to the title of 7th Lord Mohun on 23 May 1521.1 He succeeded to the title of 4th Lord Stanley [E., 1456] on 23 May 1521. He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Derby [E., 1485] on 23 M
2 CONC ay 1521. He succeeded to the title of 11th Lord Strange, of Knokyn on 23 May 1521. He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Bath (K.B.) in 1533. He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) in 1547. He held the office 
2 CONC of Lord-Lieutenant of Lancashire between 1552 and 1572.1 He held the office of Lord High Steward in 1553. He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) in 1553. He held the office of Vice-Admiral of Lancashire and Cheshire between 
2 CONC 1553 and 1569. He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) in 1558. He held the office of Chamberlain of Chester between 1559 and 1565. He held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of Cheshire between 1569 and 1572.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of Derby
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Margaret Stanley d. 1586
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of Derby and Lady Dorothy Howard
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Jane Stanley d. c Aug 1569
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Stanley, 4th Earl of Derby d. 25 Sep 1593
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Stanley d. 1576
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Anne Stanley
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Stanley d. 3 Sep 1609
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Elizabeth Stanley
