1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT '''Mary Fiennes, Baroness Dacre (1524–1576; née Mary Neville) was the daughter''' of George Nevill, 5th Baron Bergavenny by his third wife, Lady Mary Stafford, youngest daughter of Edward Stafford, 3rd Duke of Buckingham.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She married Thomas Fiennes, 9th Baron Dacre''' (c. 1515-1541), who was convicted of the murder of a gamekeeper and hanged as a common criminal at Tyburn in 1541. '''The family was stripped of its lands and titles by Henry VIII.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In the following years, Mary battled to have the properties restored on behalf of her children, and on her ascension in 1558 Elizabeth restored the title of Baron Dacre to Mary's second son''' Gregory, '''her eldest son''' Thom
2 CONC as having died of the plague at age 15.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By her first husband, Lady Dacre was the mother of:
2 CONT *Thomas Fiennes (1538–1553)
2 CONT *Gregory Fiennes, 10th Baron Dacre (1539–1594)
2 CONT *Margaret Fiennes, 11th Baroness Dacre (1540–1611)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Dacre married twice after her first husband's death and had several other children about whom little is known.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Dacre is the sitter in two significant portraits by Hans Eworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be 1502 at Abergavenny, Monmouthshire, Wales (unattested).
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of death have also been (erroneously?) reported to be December 18, 1565 at London, Middlesex (now Greater London), England (unattested).
2 CONT
