1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alice Poynes, daughter of John Poynes of com. Glocester, married 1) John Skinner of Reigate  in com Surrey, ob. s.p.; 2) Sir Thomas Palmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''1605 22 Aug being Thursday dyed Alce sometime the wife of Mr John Skynner of Rigate and lastly the wife of Sir Thomas Palmer of Angmering died at Arundel and buryed the Fryday the 23rd;'' (recorded in the parish register of St M
2 CONC ary Reigate); the parish register for Angmering records 'Lady Alice Palmere wife of Sir Thomas Palmere knight buryed'.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Poyntz, married (1st) before 1528 Elizabeth Browne. They had two sons, Henry and Matthew, and one daughter, Frideswide. He married (2nd) 1 May 1544, Margaret Saunders. They had two sons, Robert and William, and two daughters,
2 CONC  Alice (wife of John Skinner and Thomas Palmer, Knt.) and Elizabeth (wife of George Elyot).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # ''The visitations of the county of Surrey : made and taken in the years 1530 by Thomas Benolte, Clarenceux king of arms ; 1572 by Robert Cooke, Clarenceux king of arms ; and 1623 by Samuel Thompson, Windsor herald, and Augustin 
2 CONC Vincent, Rouge croix pursuivant, marshals and deputies to William Camden, Clarenceux king of arms''.  Page 59 “Skinner” < [https://archive.org/details/visitationsofcou43beno/page/58/mode/2up?q=skinner Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT # ''The Visitations of Surrey, 1530, 1572 and 1623''.  “Reigate Parish Church” In the p'ish church of Rigate in Com' Surrey taken 6 Aprill 1623.  page 109-110.  < [https://archive.org/details/visitationsofcou43beno/page/110/mode/2
2 CONC up Archive.Org] >  'in the body of the church upon a gravestone in brass' epitaph to John Skinner.  This monument was erected by Allice one of the Daughters of Jo. Poyntz of Alderley in the County of Gloster in memory of her louei
2 CONC ng husband John Skinner Esqr one of the Clarke Controulers of the Houshould to the high & mighty Princes Queene Elizebeth wch John deceased the 19 day of May An0 1584.
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Alice (Poyntz) Palmer (bef.1544-1605)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Poyntz-305 : accessed 24 April 2024). cites 
