1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary of Guise, Queen consort of Scots; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Consort in Scotland 4 August 1534 - 9 June 1537
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 May 1538 – 14 December 1542 
2 CONT
2 CONT Coronation 22 February 1540 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Louis II, Duke of Longueville
2 CONT
2 CONT James V of Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Claude, Duke of Guise 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother Antoinette of Bourbon-Vendôme
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 22 November 1515
2 CONT
2 CONT Bar-le-Duc, Lorraine, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 11 June 1560 (aged 44) (dropsy)
2 CONT
2 CONT Edinburgh Castle, Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Saint Pierre de Reims, France 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mary of Guise (French: Marie; 22 November 1515 – 11 June 1560) was queen of Scotland as the second spouse of King James V. She was the mother of Mary, Queen of Scots, and served as regent of Scotland in her daughter's name from 1
2 CONC 554 to 1560. A native of Lorraine, she was a member of the powerful House of Guise, which played a prominent role in 16th-century French politics."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================================================================================
