2 CONT [http://www.notablebiographies.com/Ma-Mo/Medici-Catherine-de.html '''Catherine de' Medici Biography''']
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1533 Pope Clement arranged the marriage of fourteen-year-old Catherine to fourteen-year-old Henry, the duke of Orleans and younger son of King Francis I (1494–1547) of France. Catherine eventually gave birth to ten children, be
2 CONC ginning in 1543. The death of her husband's older brother in 1536 made Henry and Catherine next in line for the throne. Catherine's husband, now '''Henry II, had been cared for at age eleven''' by '''Diane de Poitiers''', who was 
2 CONC twenty years his senior. Despite this age difference, they became lovers, and throughout most of Henry's reign as king of France, which began in 1547,
2 CONT
2 CONT Diane had more influence over him than Catherine did. Diane was even given responsibility for raising Catherine's children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Read more: http://www.notablebiographies.com/Ma-Mo/Medici-Catherine-de.html#ixzz3xBMQC0tJ
2 CONT
