1 NOTE Called Sigismund Augustus.  He was also grand duke of Lithuania (1544-69). 
2 CONT  Sigismund II was crowned king in 1530 but did not actually succeed to the 
2 CONT throne until his father's death 18 years later. Like his father, he allied 
2 CONT himself with the great magnate families and was at odds with the szlachta 
2 CONT (gentry) class. Although Roman Catholic, he did little to prevent the 
2 CONT spread of Protestantism, which flourished in Poland and Lithuania during 
2 CONT his reign. In 1559 he added Livonia to his domains, and ten years later, 
2 CONT by the Union of Lublin, he formally united Poland and Lithuania, ending 
2 CONT the existence of the latter as a separate duchy. Sigismund died childless, 
2 CONT and with him the Jagiellon dynasty came to an end.
1 NOTE KING OF POLAND AS SIGISMUND II 1548-1572
