1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lady Jane Grey (c. 1537 – 12 February 1554), also known as Lady Jane Dudley (after her marriage) and as '''"the Nine Days' Queen"''', was an English noblewoman and''' de facto Queen of England and Ireland from 10 J
2 CONC uly until 19 July 1553.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT After Edward's death, Jane was proclaimed queen on 10 July 1553 and awaited coronation in the Tower of London. Support for Mary grew very quickly, and most of Jane's supporters abandoned her. The Privy Council of England suddenly 
2 CONC changed sides and proclaimed Mary as queen on 19 July 1553, deposing Jane. Her primary supporter, her father-in-law the Duke of Northumberland, was accused of treason and executed less than a month later. Jane was held prisoner at
2 CONC  the Tower and was convicted in November 1553 of high treason, which carried a sentence of death—though Mary initially spared her life. However, Jane soon became viewed as a threat to the Crown when her father, Henry Grey, 1st Duk
2 CONC e of Suffolk, got involved with Wyatt's rebellion against Queen Mary's intention to marry Philip II of Spain. Both Jane and her husband were executed on 12 February 1554.{{https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/95/Lady_Jane_%
2 CONC 281986_film%29_poster.jpg|right|65px}}
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady_Jane_Grey
2 CONT
2 CONT *'' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady_Jane_(1986_film)_   Available a pretty 1986 British costume-drama romance film of her story] ''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.bing.com/videos/search?q=Lady+Jane+Grey+Ghost&&view=detail&mid=E184E0AE8B83874D124AE184E0AE8B83874D124A&&FORM=VRDGAR ''Prayer Book'']
2 CONT
2 CONT ======================================Biography========================================
2 CONT '''Lady Jane Grey, Queen of England (disputed)''' was born circa October 12, 1537 in Bradgate Park, Charwood Forest, Leicestershire, England. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-8861467 Henry Grey, 1st Duke of Suffolk, 
2 CONC 3rd Marquess of Dorset] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-3360561 Frances Brandon, Duchess of Suffolk]. She was a Queen of England, Queen of England for 9 days, Queen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane married [https://www.geni.com/profile-14162292 Lord Guilford Dudley] on May 21, 1553 in Durham House,London,England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 12, 1554 in Tower Green, inside the Tower of London, England from Execution and was buried in 1554 in Chapel of St Peter-ad-Vincula, London Borough of Tower Hamlets, Greater London, England, United Kingdom. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT The question of whether or not she was actually queen hinges on her legal standing.  Though Edward had named her as his successor, the laws of succession, as ratified by Parliament in 1543,had established the line as going to Mary
2 CONC  and then Elizabeth, and the king had no right to change the succession without the consent of Parliament. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Find-a-Grave Memorial #1971,  Chapel of Saint Peter-ad-Vincula, London Borough of Tower Hamlets, Greater London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------- 
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10152.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Jane Grey was born in October 1537 at Bradgate Manor, Bradgate, Leicestershire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was also reported to have been born in 1536. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Sir Henry Grey, 1st Duke of Suffolk and Lady Frances Brandon. She married Lord Guilford Dudley, son of John Dudley, 1st Duke of Northumberland and Jane Guilford, on 21 May 1553.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 12 February 1554 at age 16 executed.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was buried at Church of St. Peter-ad-Vincula, London Borough of Tower Hamlets, Greater London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Jane Grey gained the title of Queen Jane I of England on 10 July 1553.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was deposed as Queen of England on 19 July 1553.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT She has an extensive biographical entry in the Dictionary of National Biography.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations:
