1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Documents
2 CONT Reference:	C 1/1330/52-57 <br/>
2 CONT Description:  <br/>
2 CONT Short title: Bosgrave v Fytz. <br/>
2 CONT Plaintiffs: '''Leonard BOSGRAVE and Joan his wife, daughter of Thomas Arundell, knight, attainted of felony, and late the wife of Robert Fytz James'''. <br/>
2 CONT Defendants: James FYTZ JAMES, knight, and Richard FYTZ JAMES, gentleman. <br/>
2 CONT Subject: Keepership of the park of Evercreech demised by the bishop of Bath and Wells to '''Nicholas Fytz James, esquire, father of the said Robert'''. Somerset <br/>
2 CONT Date:	1553-1555 <br/>
2 CONT Held by:	[http://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/C7500937 The National Archives, Kew] <br/>
2 CONT Legal status:	Public Record(s) <br/>
2 CONT Closure status:	Open Document, Open Description <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 Feb. 1560 <br/>
2 CONT Grant to Jane Bosgrove, widow, of the wardship and marriage of Nicholas Bosgrove, son an heir of Leonard Bosgrove; with an annuity of 4l. from 30 Nov., 4 and 5 Ph. & Mary, when John died. Yearly value of the inheritance 19l. 5s. 4
2 CONC d. <br/>
2 CONT Source: [https://archive.org/stream/calendarofpatent01grea_0#page/341/mode/1up Calendar of the patent rolls preserved in the Public Record Office: Elizabeth, Part VI., Page 341]
