2 CONT **ARUNDELL OF WARDOUR.
2 CONT *Pg.4
2 CONT *Sir Thomas Arundell of Sheftsbury, 2 son. Sheriff of Dorsetshire 22 and 23 Hen. VIII. Beheaded 26 Feb. 1553. Inq. p.m., 6 Edw. VI. Pt. 2, No. 77. Named in his father's will, son of Sir John Arundell & Eleanor Gray; marr. Margaret
2 CONC , da. and coh. of Lord Edmond Howard and sister of Queen Catherine, 5 wife of K. Hen. VIII. Named in Inq. taken after her husband's death. She died 10 Oct. 1562. parents of (pg.7 Sir Matthew (m. Margaret Willoughby), '''Sir Charle
2 CONC s''', Margaret (m. Sir Henry Weston), Dorothy, Jane (m. Sir William Bevill) Arundell)
2 CONT *Pg.7
2 CONT *'''Sir Charles Arundell, of the City of London, 2 son, named after Charles Emperor of Germany by Philip II of Spain, his godfather. This King knighted him, and when he fled from England allowed him "0 crowns monthly for his maint
2 CONC enance. Named in will of his aunt Jane Arundell, 1577. Died in Paris 9 Dec. 1587. s.p., his brother Sir Matthew his heir. Inq. p.m. 30 Eliz., Pt. 1, No 89. The Inq. names his father and mother and two sisters, Dorothy and Jane.
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Godson of Philp II of Spain (who of course was also KIng of England during Mary's reign), who named him after Emperor Charles of Germany. Was also knighted by Philip II, who paid him 80 crowns annually for maintenance after he fle
2 CONC d from England during Elizabeth I's reign.
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
