1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ADAM STEWART ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sometime Factor of Charterhouse, afterwards Pensioner of Charterhouse===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adam Stewart is the bastard son of James V, King of Scots : "filius illustrisimi principis Jacobi  quinti  scotorum regis" [http://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/archiveDS/archiveDownload?t=arch-352-1/dissemination/pdf/vol_053/53
2 CONC _180_195.pdf Proceedings of the Society of Antiquaries, May 12th 1919: Some further Orkney Armorials, page 186] His mother was Helenor Stewart (aka Elizabeth Stewart), daughter of John, Earl of Lennox. His date of his birth is not
2 CONC  known. [Peter D. Andersen, Robert Stewart, Earl of Stewart, Lord of Shetland, 1533-1593 (John Donald, Edinburgh, 1982), p. 157]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adam Stewart died in Orkney on 20 June 1575 .[Peter D. Andersen, Robert Stewart, Earl of Stewart, Lord of Shetland, 1533-1593 (John Donald, Edinburgh, 1982), p. 157] He was buried in St. Magnus Cathedral in Kirkwall, where his 
2 CONC daughter Barbara Stewart raised a tombstone. [http://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/archiveDS/archiveDownload?t=arch-352-1/dissemination/pdf/vol_053/53_180_195.pdf Proceedings of the Society of Antiquaries, May 12th 1919: Some furth
2 CONC er Orkney Armorials, page 186]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Monumental Inscription in St. Magnus Cathedral, Kirkwall ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adamus . steuardus . filius . illustrisimi . principis . Jacobi . quinti . scotorum . regis . qui . obit . vicesimo ‘ die . junii . anno . domini . m . v . lxxv .  [words along the edge follow] domina – de -  halcro – filia – e
2 CONC jusdem – fieri – hac – sepulchrum – et – at least two words missing [http://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk/archiveDS/archiveDownload?t=arch-352-1/dissemination/pdf/vol_053/53_180_195.pdf Proceedings of the Society of Antiquaries, Ma
2 CONC y 12th 1919: Some further Orkney Armorials, page 186]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adam Stewart married Janet Ruthven, daughter of William Ruthven of Ballendean. [Peter D. Andersen, Robert Stewart, Earl of Stewart, Lord of Shetland, 1533-1593 (John Donald, Edinburgh, 1982), pp. 71, 80, 104, biographical detai
2 CONC ls, 156-8]  [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft#page/101/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, iv, page 101] After the death of her husband Janet Ruthven was granted a pension of fifty pounds and a quantity of victual fro
2 CONC m the thirds of the Charterhouse not assigned to ministers. At this time she is said to have been 'gritlie burdynit with mony bairnis and not being providir for.' The terms of this gift were later changed and the money doubled, on
2 CONC e of the reasons for the assistance being that the 'bairnis' were 'so tender of bluid unto him as his majestie man be cairful that sum relief may be had unto thame.' [Peter D. Anderson, Robert Stewart Earl of Orlney Lord of Shetla
2 CONC nd 1533-1593 (John Donald, Edinburgh, 1982), page 158 where Anderson cites the Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, vii, numbers 1003 and 2316]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''When Adam Stewart died in 1575 his widow is said to have been: "gritlie burdynnit with mony bairnis." [Registrum Secreti sigilli, 1575–80, no. 1003] However, the names of only three daughters have been identified:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Barbara-Stewart/6000000006290219237
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Elspeth-Stewart/6000000057005498988?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529541263639&through=6000000002188113095
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Katheryne-Stewart/6000000195228486868?through=6000000034187124582
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Dorathie-Stewart/6000000079446073749?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529541359921&through=6000000002188113095
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Jane-Stewart/6000000195228973878?through=6000000034187124582
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Testament Dative and Inventory of his wife ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Janet Ruthven, died intestate on 20 January 1606. Her testament dative and inventory was given up on 22 February 1606 by her daughter Elspeth Stewart. At the time of her mother's death, she and her mother were residents of the 
2 CONC City of Perth. Elspeth Stewart, who was her mother's only executor dative, may have been the only child still in life. Certainly, no financial provision was made for any others. Confirmation was granted to Elspeth Stewart on 8 Mar
2 CONC ch 1606. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Edinburgh, testament Dative of Jonet Ruthwen, relict of Adame Stewart [prior] of Charterhous, reference CC8/8/41 folios 333-34]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000057005594217& Image of Testament Dative p. 333] 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000057005594219& Image of Testament Dative p. 334]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1540-41: Instrument containing process of ratification by John Williamson, provost of collegiate church of Seiton, and Adam Stewart, canon of the cathedral church of Orkney, judges delegate appointed by Anthony, card
2 CONC inal priest of SS Quatuor Coronati, of feu charter, 18 Jan 1539/1540, by Andrew, abbot of Melrose, and the convent thereof, in favour of William Linlithqw, son of deceased David Linlithqw, in liferent, and John Linlithqw, his son 
2 CONC and apparent heir, in fee. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD47%2f25&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=adam+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Leith-Buchanan 
2 CONC of Ross and Drummakil, reference GD47/25]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 July 1556: Tack by Dean Adam Forman, prior of Charterhouse called the Vale of Virtue beside burgh of Perth, with consent of convent thereof, to Colin Campbell of Glenurquhay and Katherine Ruthven, his spouse, and Duncan Campb
2 CONC ell, their son and apparent heir, of lands of Artollonyth with miln thereof, fishings on Lochtay, and lands of Ballacrag, in lordship of Glendochard, sheriffdom of Perth, for 6 years. Witnesses: Patrick, lord Ruthven, Mr Alexander
2 CONC  Levingstoun of Doanypace, William Moncreif of that ilk, Sir Robert Forman of Luthry, kt., Lyon king of arms, George Johneson, burgess of Perth, Robert Rollok and Henry Eldar, chaplains and notaries. Applied papered common seal of
2 CONC  Charterhouse, damaged. Signed by granter and members of conven sir John Burnat, sir Walter Touris, ? treasurer, sir John Syme, procurator, sir Andrew Blythman, sir James Meak, vicar, sir William Clapene, sir Alexander Calland and
2 CONC  sir Adam Stewart [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f1%2f100&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=adam+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell
2 CONC  Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reerence GD112/1/100]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 August 1559: Accounts of Custumars and Bailies of Burghs, rendered at Edinburgh, A. D. 1560. Computum Thome Scot, custumarii de Perth redditum per eundum, [Edinburgh, 26 September 1560, from 21 August 1559. Charge £126, grea
2 CONC t custom of said burgh by tack to accountant, date 6 September 1558. Discharge. To comptroller, £10. To prior and convent of Charterhouse, by receipt of Adame Stewarte, alleged to be factor thereof, £26.13s.4d. To prior and conven
2 CONC t of St. Andrews, 40s. [https://archive.org/stream/exchequerrollss03exchgoog#page/n189/mode/1up George Powell McNeill, M.A., LL.B. (editor), Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorm. The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland, xix, A. D. 1557-1567, pa
2 CONC ge 109]'''
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 February 1572-73: An additional copy of a harter by George Balfour with an extra signature "Adam Stewart'" and granter's personal seal also attached. The charter follows:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Charter by George Balfour, prior of carthusian house called Vallis virtutis formerly situated near burgh of Perth, and convent thereof, to Colin Campbell of Glenurquhard and Katherine Ruthven, his spouse, in liferent, and to Du
2 CONC ncan Campbell, their son and apparent heir, in fee, of 3 merkland of Kirktoun of Killin, 20s land of Badnacarrie, 20s land of Craignevin, 6 merkland of Kinyaldy with island called Ilanrane, 2 merkland of Qucharne, 2 merkland of Ar
2 CONC tnagald Eister, 1 merkland of Artnagald Wester, 20s land of Soy, 3 merkland of Incheschewin, lands of Artollony with fishing on Lochtay, lands of Ballacraig, with office of bailie, in lordship of Glendochard, sheriffdom of Perth, 
2 CONC 6 February 1572/3.Seal of convent, poor impression, on tag.Signed by granter, James Sym and Andrew Blythtman.Witnesses: Mr George Boswall, chirurgian, Alexander Anderson, Andrew Brydy, burgesses of Perth, William Dundas and Mr Geo
2 CONC rge Quhyt. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f45%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Adam+Stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Charterhouse of Perth, ref
2 CONC erence GD112/2/45/1]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 December 1573: Instrument of sasine following from a charter by James, Bishop of Dunkeld. Witnesses: Patrick Eviot of Balhoussy, Andrew Marsar, bailie, Adam Stewart, pensioner of Chartarhouss, David Murray, Gavin Hammiltoun,
2 CONC  Dougal Campbell, servants of said Colin, Alexander Quhite, George Bow, burgesses, and William Ross, sergeant of said burgh. Seal on tag. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f13
2 CONC 0&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=adam+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), Titles to Particular Lands, reference GD112/2/1
2 CONC 30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Some Source References ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_V_of_Scotland Wikipedia: James V, King of Scots]
2 CONT # [http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00007579&tree=LEO Genealogics: Adam Stewart]
2 CONT # [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prior_of_Perth Wikipedia: Prior of Perth]
2 CONT # [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perth_Charterhouse Wikipedia: Perth Charterhouse]
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stewart-4377
2 CONT * https://gw.geneanet.org/debbieduncan?lang=en&n=stewart&p=adam
2 CONT * https://www.stewartsociety.org/history-of-the-stewarts.cfm?section=family-lines&subcatid=43&histid=159
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/105504509/adam-stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Stewart was the first illegitimate son of King James V of Scotland, with his mother being Lady Elizabeth Stewart, who was the daughter of Lady Eleanor Sinclair and Sir John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox and 1st Earl of Atholl. 
2 CONC Lady Elizabeth Stewart subsequently married (1) William, Earl of Erroll; m2. John Gordon, 11th Earl of Sutherland in 1549.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam was the Prior of the Charterhouse - he was given this sinecure by his father King James V as a source of income, a common practice among the gentry, peerage and royalty of the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 11, 1559, the Perth Charterhouse and the other religious houses of Perth were attacked and destroyed by Protestant "reformers". One of the brothers was killed, four others fled abroad, while six monks chose to remain; two o
2 CONC f those, then fled into foreign Carthusian houses in 1567. Of the four who remained in 1567, one was Adam Stewart.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the Reformation Adam Stewart married Janet Ruthven; they are commemorated on a memorial stone at Kirkwall Cathedral in Orkney, set up by their daughter Barbara Halcro (née Stewart), wife of Henry Halcro of that Ilk (ie. of H
2 CONC alcro) in the southernmost part of the Orkney mainland.
