1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ROBERT STEWART, EARL OF ORKNEY, LORD OF SHETLAND===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart is the bastard son of James V, King of Scots, and Euphemia Elphinestone. He and his mother are mentioned in the entail of a charter by which his father the king confirmed that he had given the lands of Temptallou
2 CONC n and others to his bastard son James Stewart by Margaret Erskine: "Rob. S. ejus fratri, filio naturali inter regem et Eufamiam Elphinstoun procreato." The charter was issued under the Great Seal of Scotland on 31 August 1536. [ht
2 CONC tps://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/360/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 1620 on pp. 360-61]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart was born in the Spring of 1533, probably between 14 February and 4 June 1533. His place of birth is not known. [Peter D. Andersen, Robert Stewart, Earl of Orkney, Lord of Shetland, 1533-1593 (John Donald, Edinbur
2 CONC gh, 1982), pp. 154-5] For a discussion about his date of birth see [https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/12812992.pdf Earl Robert Stewart and his Administration in Orkney and Shetland 1564-93 by Peter D. Anderson]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 22 December 1539 five and one half elns of red velvet were delivered to Thomas Arthur, the king's tailor, in order to make a coat for Robert Stewart, the king's son.  [https://archive.org/stream/accountslordhig00treagoog#pag
2 CONC e/n323/mode/1up Accounts of the Lord High Treasurers of Scotland, A.D. 1538-1541, vii, p. 265]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart's mother was married to John Bruce of Cultmalindie in 1540. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/572/mode/1up The Scots Peerage] Francis J. Grant says that she married for a second time to 
2 CONC John Bruce of Kennet. [https://archive.org/stream/TheCountyFamiliesOfTheShetlandIslands/The%20County%20Families%20of%20the%20Shetland%20Islands#page/n12/mode/1up The County Families of the Island of Shetland] Cultmalindie is not l
2 CONC ocated in the Shetland islands, it is located in the Perthshire parish of Tibbermore.[http://www.visionofbritain.org.uk/place/16346 A Vision of Britain Through Time] Euphame Elphinestone's son Laurence Bruce of Cultmalindie was th
2 CONC e first member of his family to go to Shetland, where he was appointed underfowde by Robert Stewart, his brother uterine, but he did not go there until 1571. [https://archive.org/stream/TheCountyFamiliesOfTheShetlandIslands/The%20
2 CONC County%20Families%20of%20the%20Shetland%20Islands#page/n12/mode/1up The County Families of the Islands of Shetland]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Feuar of the Crown Lands of Orkney and Shetland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 25 May 1565 the the crown lands of Orkney and Shetland were conferred on Sir Robert Stewart of Strathdon. [https://archive.org/stream/TheCountyFamiliesOfTheShetlandIslands/The%20County%20Families%20of%20the%20Shetland%20Isla
2 CONC nds#page/n3/mode/1up The County Families of the Shetland Islands] Robert Stewart is noticed in that style, as the feuar of the lands and lordship of Orkney and Shetland, and as sheriff principal of the same, in a summons issued by
2 CONC  him in Orkney on 4 November 1567.  [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/123/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Earl of Orkney, Lord of Shetland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart was created Earl of Orkney and Lord of Shetland by a patent dated 28 October 1581.[https://archive.org/stream/TheCountyFamiliesOfTheShetlandIslands/The%20County%20Families%20of%20the%20Shetland%20Islands#page/n3/
2 CONC mode/1up The County Families of the Shetland Islands]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart, Earl of Orkney and Lord of Shetland died on 4 February 1593. He died in his palace at Kirkwall in Orkney. He made his last will and testament two days before, from his death bed in his palace in Kirkwall. Presen
2 CONC t to witness his final act was his daughter Jean and her husband Lord Lindores, his natural son James Stewart of Graemsay, Thomas Swinton, minister at Kirkwall, Walter Bruce, sheriff clerk, and two Edinburgh Burgesses, John Dick a
2 CONC nd David Pringle. [Peter D. Andersen, Robert Stewart, Earl of Orkney, Lord of Shetland, 1533-1593 (John Donald, Edinburgh, 1982), page 129] [https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/12812992.pdf Earl Robert Stewart and his Aministration in
2 CONC  Orkney and Shetland 1564-93 by Peter D. Anderson]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Burial ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It has been suggested that Earl Robert Stewart was buried in St. Magnus Cathedral in Kirkwall.  [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=84549118 Find A Grave Memorial] However, the comprehensive list of tombs in 
2 CONC the RCAHMS Inventory makes no mention of a tomb for Earl Robert.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
