1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Stewart was born illegitimately between 1528 and 1542. She was the daughter of James V Stewart, King of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#JamesVdied1542B King James V had one illegitimate daughter by Mistress (9):
2 CONT
2 CONT 12.       MARGARET Stewart .  Balfour Paul records King James’s daughter “Margaret...mentioned in a contract in the charter-chest of the Earl of Home, wherein the Master of Home is proposed as her husband” (no mother named)[1596].
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT [1596] Balfour Paul Scots Peerage, Vol. I, p. 25, citing “Hist. MSS. Comm. Report, xiii. App. viii. 80 and 94”. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/25/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 25]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://www.thepeerage.com/p10836.htm#i108351 cites 
2 CONT ## [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 242. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT ## [S323] Sir James Balfour Paul, ''The Scots Peerage: founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's The Peerage of Scotland'' (Edinburgh, Scotland: David Douglas, 1904), volume I, page 25. Hereinafter cited as The Scots Peera
2 CONC ge. < [https://books.google.com/books?id=_KEKAAAAIAAJ&vq=%E2%80%9CMargaret%20Stewart%E2%80%9D&pg=PA25#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks] > 
