1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth was stillborn. Frances Brandon and Adrian Carew would go on to name another daughter Elizabeth the next year, but she too would die young.
2 CONT
2 CONT from the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frances_Grey,_Duchess_of_Suffolk#Second_marriage_and_death Wikipedia] page of Frances Brandon:
2 CONT
2 CONT She and Stokes married in 1555.[10] Three children were born to the couple:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Elizabeth Stokes (20 November 1554), stillborn.
2 CONT * Elizabeth Stokes (16 July 1555 – 7 February 1556), died in infancy.
2 CONT * A son (December, 1556), stillborn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source [10]: ''Lady Jane Grey: A Tudor Mystery'' by Eric Ives, 2009
