2 CONT *'''Elizabeth NEVILLE
2 CONT *'''Born: ABT 1550
2 CONT *'''Died: 1630
2 CONT *Notes: he was an ancestor of the biographer John Aubrey who recorded that '''she “had Chaucer at her fingers’ ends” and “understood jewels as well as any jeweler” as well as being about to “manage her estate as well as any man”. 
2 CONC Elizabeth married Sir John Danvers of Dauntsey, Wiltshire. Their children were''' Sir Charles, Lucy, Sir Henry, Elizabeth, Eleanor, Anne, Catherine, Mary, John, and Dorothy. In Oct 1595, Charles and Henry were forced to flee the c
2 CONC ountry following the murder of Henry Long, a member of the family with whom the Danvers family had been feuding for some time. '''In order to facilitate obtaining pardons for them, Elizabeth married Sir Edmund Carey, Queen Elizabe
2 CONC th’s cousin'''. Shortly thereafter, Sir Charles was allowed to return to England. Sir Henry was pardoned a bit later. In 1601, however, Charles was again in need of a pardon, but this time his crime was conspiring with the Earl of
2 CONC  Essex and '''although his mother offered to pay £10,000 for his release, he was executed for treason.
2 CONT *Father: John NEVILLE (4º B. Latimer)
2 CONT *Mother: Lucy SOMERSET (B. Latimer)
2 CONT *'''Married 1: John DANVERS of Dauntsey (Sir Knight)''' (See his Biography) (son of Sylvester Danvers of Dauntsey and Elizabeth Mordaunt)
