2 CONT His daughters were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Lady Catherine Cecil (d. unm.)
2 CONT * 2. Lady Lucy Cecil (b. 7 Mar 1567/8; d. Oct 1614), mar. 28 Feb 1586/7 John [Paulet], 4th Marquess of Winchester, and had issue
2 CONT * 3. Lady Mildred Cecil, mar. (1) Sir Thomas Read, and (2) as his second wife Sir Edmund Trafford, of Trafford Park, co. Lancaster (d. May 1620), and had issue by her second husband
2 CONT * 4. Lady Mary Cecil (b. 15 Jul 1573; bur. 18 Mar 1637/8), mar. c. 1590 Edward [Denny], 1st Earl of Norwich, and had issue
2 CONT * 5. Lady Susan Cecil (d. unm.)
2 CONT * 6. Lady Elizabeth Cecil, mar. (1) Sir William Hatton, and (2) as his second wife Sir Edward Coke, Chief Justice of the Common Pleas, and had issue by her second husband
2 CONT * 7. Lady Dorothy Cecil (bapt. 11 Aug 1577; bur. 11 Nov 1613), mar. as his first wife Sir Giles Alington, of Horseheath, co. Cambridge (bapt. 18 Sep 1572; bur. 23 Dec 1638), son of Giles Alington, of Horseheath, co. Cambridge, by 
2 CONC his wife Margaret Spencer, 3rd dau. of Sir John Spencer, of Wormleighton, co. Warwick, and Althorp, co. Northampton, and had issue
2 CONT * 8. Lady Frances Cecil (bapt. 25 Feb 1580/1; d. 12 Jun 1653), mar. bef. 3 Sep 1602 Nicholas [Tufton], 1st Earl of Thanet, and had issue mar. (2) c.1610 Hon Frances Smith (widow of Sir Thomas Smith, Master of Requests to King Jame
2 CONC s I;  d. 1663), dau. of William [Brydges], 4th Baron Chandos, by his wife Mary Hopton, dau. of Sir Owen Hopton only child by second wife
2 CONT * 9. Lady Anne Cecil (dvp. Sep 1621)
