1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Katherine Neville,''' ''Countess of Northumberland'', was born in 1546, Snape Hall, Snape, Yorkshire, England and died on 28 October 1596. She was buried in Saint Paul's Chapel, Westminster Abbey, Westminster, L
2 CONC ondon, England.  From before 25 January 1562, her married name became ''Percy''. From 1588, her married name became ''Fitton''.  She was also known as ''Catherine Neville''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  daughter of John Neville, (ca. 1520-1577) 4th Lord Latymer and Lucy Somerset (?-ca.1582). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # before 25 January 1562, to Henry Percy (ca. 1532-1585), 2nd Earl of Northumberland (''AKA 8th Earl Northumberland''), son of Sir Thomas Percy and Eleanor Harbottle.
2 CONT # in 1588, Snape Hall, Snape, Yorkshire, England, to Francis Fitton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Katherine Neville and Henry Percy:
2 CONT # Henry Percy (9º E. Northumberland) (1564-1632), married Lady Doroty Devereux.
2 CONT # Thomas Percy
2 CONT # William Percy
2 CONT # Charles Percy (Sir)
2 CONT # Lucy Percy, married 1st to Sir John Wotton;  2nd to Sir Hugh Owen
2 CONT # Richard Percy
2 CONT # Joscelyne Percy (Sir)
2 CONT # Anne Percy
2 CONT # Alan Percy (Sir) d. married Mary Fitz
2 CONT # Eleanor Percy (1583-1650) married William Herbert, 1st Baron of Powis
2 CONT # George Percy (Sir) (1580-1632) married Anne Floyd
2 CONT
