2 CONC  M30/62; C78/473/2, 14. 53. PROB 11/161, f. 243. 54. Jones, 14. 55. PROB 11/161, ff. 241-3v. 56. M. Robbins, ‘Gentry of S.E. Glam. 1540-1640’ (Cardiff Univ. Ph.D. thesis, 1974), iii. plates 31, 32.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir  Thomas  Mansel (d. 163),  baronet, held the offices of sheriff  and knight of the shire  for Glamorgan  and one of whose sons was ARTHUR  MANSEL, father of Bussy  Mansel (q.v.)  , was succeeded by his eldest son,  Sir  LEWIS 
2 CONC MANSEL (d. 1638)
2 CONT
2 CONT Served as High Sheriff of Margam twice in 1594 and 1604.
