2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Jane Radcliffe Browne was never Viscountess Montague, she died in 1552 and Browne was not created a viscount until 1554
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === !Plantagenet Ancestry of Seventeenth-Cen ===
2 CONT !Plantagenet Ancestry of Seventeenth-Century Colonists The Descent from the Later Plantagenet Kings of England, Henry III, Edward I, Edward II, and Edward III, of Emigrants from England and Wales to the North American Colonies bef
2 CONC ore 1701 by David Faris. First Edition
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Life Sketch ===
2 CONT Jane Radcliffe was the daughter of Robert Radcliffe, 1st Earl of Sussex, and his second wife, Margaret Stanley, daughter of Thomas Stanley, 2nd Earl of Derby.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Radcliffe married Anthony Browne, 1st Viscount Montagu,  the oldest son of Sir Anthony Browne and his first wife, Alice Gage. Anthony Browne was not Viscount Montagu at the time of their marriage, therefore, Jane Radcliffe Br
2 CONC owne was never Viscountess Montague as she died before her husband attained his title.  Unfortunately, Jane died in childbed, giving birth to twins  born 22 July 1552 at Cowdray House.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Of Childhood Fever Jane Radcliffe, daugh ===
2 CONT Of Childhood Fever Jane Radcliffe, daughter of Robert Radcliff,LordFitzWalter, 1st Earl of Sussex,(Descendant of King EdwardI), by Margaret(Descendant of King Edward III0, daughter ofThomas Stanley, Earl ofDerby,
2 CONT
