3 CITY Ormskirk
3 STAE England
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mixes up Anne (Starkey) Blundell with her step sister, Anne (Stanley) Sutton 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/stanley/4105/
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Stanley, wife of Edward Sutton, is not the daughter of Peter Stanley, Esq., (d. 1592) of Bickerstaffe and Moor Hall by his second wife Cecily Tarleton.That Anne was married to a man named - Blundell sometime before 1589.
2 CONT
2 CONT This part of Lancashire was notorious for allowing child marriages, where patriarchs controlled the destiny of their heirs by marrying them at young ages [even as early as five] to control the distribution of their estates.When Ed
2 CONC ward Stanley, Esq. (d. 1610) died, his son and heir was only eleven years old and already married.
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe this is the case as well for Anne Stanley, Gent. , wife of Edward Sutton.I believe I can build a strong case for identifying her as a child of Henry Stanley, Esq. (d. 1598) of Bickerstaffe, Little Hall, and Cross Hall, b
2 CONC y his wife Mrs Margaret Stanley (d. 1613), daughter of Peter Stanley, Esq.(d. 1592) by his first wife Elizabeth Scarisbrick (1516-1558).
