1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk==
2 CONT '''Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk (third creation), KG Earl Marshal (10 March 1536 – 2 June 1572) was an English nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Howard was the son of the poet Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey. He was taught as a child by John Foxe, the Protestant martyrologist, who remained a lifelong recipient of Howard's patronage. His father predeceased him and so Thomas
2 CONC  inherited the Dukedom of Norfolk upon the death of his grandfather, the 3rd Duke of Norfolk in 1554.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Norfolk was related to Queen Elizabeth I of England through her mother's family and was trusted with public office despite his family's history and, although he claimed to be a Protestant, his prior support for the Catholic cau
2 CONC se.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==='''First wife===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Howard's first wife was Mary FitzAlan, who after the death of her brother Henry in 1556 became heiress to the Arundel Estates of her father Henry FitzAlan, 19th Earl of Arundel. She died after a year of marriage having g
2 CONC iven birth to a son Philip Howard, who later became 20th Earl of Arundel. It is from this marriage that the present Duke of Norfolk takes his name of 'FitzAlan-Howard' and why his seat is in Arundel. Though her funeral effigy is t
2 CONC here, Mary FitzAlan was never buried at Framlingham, but at the church of St. Clement Without, Temple Bar and then (under the direction of her grandson's will) at Arundel.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==='''Second wife===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas next married another heiress, Margaret daughter of Thomas Audley, 1st Baron Audley of Walden. She also died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret's children by her marriage to Norfolk were two boys and two girls. Both Mary and Margaret have their tomb effigies at St Michael the Archangel, Framlingham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==='''Third wife===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''After Margaret's death, Thomas married Elizabeth Leyburne, widow of Thomas Dacre, 4th Baron Dacre of Gillesland.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Norfolk made remarkable marriage plans whereby Elizabeth's three daughters by Dacre became the wives of the sons of his own
2 CONT
2 CONT ==='''Attempted fourth marriage, plots and death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth I imprisoned Norfolk in 1569 for scheming to marry Mary, Queen of Scots.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Following his release, he perhaps (the strength of the evidence for his participation in the Ridolfi plot is doubted by some)[citation needed] participated in the Ridolfi plot with King Philip II of Spain to put Mary on the Eng
2 CONC lish throne and restore Catholicism in England and was executed for treason in 1572. He is buried at St Peter ad Vincula at the Tower of London.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Norfolk's lands and titles were forfeited, although much of the estate was restored to his sons. The title of Duke of Norfolk was restored, four generations later, to Thomas Howard.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Howard,_4th_Duke_of_Norfolk
2 CONT *________________________
2 CONT *'''Sir Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk, Earl of Surey1
2 CONT *'''M, #80592, b. 10 March 1538, d. 2 June 1572
2 CONT *Father      Sir Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey2 b. bt 1516 - 1518, d. 19 Jan 1547
2 CONT *Mother     Frances Vere2 b. c 1517, d. 30 Jun 1577
2 CONT *'''     Sir Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk, Earl of Surey was born on 10 March 1538 at Corby Castle, Kenninghall, Norfolk, England.1 He married Mary FitzAlan, daughter of Sir Henry FitzAlan, 24th (19th) Earl of Arundel and Ca
2 CONC therine Grey, circa 30 March 1555.3 Sir Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk, Earl of Surey married Margaret Audley, daughter of Sir Thomas Audley, 1st Baron Audley of Walden and Elizabeth Grey, between 10 December 1558 and 2 March 
2 CONC 1559.4 Sir Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk, Earl of Surey married Elizabeth Leybourne, daughter of Sir James Leybourne and Helen Preston, on 29 January 1567.4 Sir Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk, Earl of Surey died on 2 June
2 CONC  1572 at Tower Hill, London, Middlesex, England, at age 34.1
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Mary FitzAlan b. c 1531, d. 25 Aug 1557
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Margaret Audley b. 1540, d. 10 Jan 1564
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Margaret Howard5 b. 1 Aug 1561, d. 19 Aug 1591
2 CONT **Sir Thomas Howard, 1st Lord Howard of Walden+6 b. 24 Aug 1561, d. 28 May 1626
2 CONT *'''Family 3      Elizabeth Leybourne b. c 1536, d. 4 Sep 1567
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. IX, p. 622-624.
2 CONT * 2.[S11572] The Lineage and Ancestry of H.R.H. Prince Charles, Prince of Wales, by Gerald Paget, Vol. II, Vol. IX, p. 622-624.
2 CONT * 3.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. IX, p. 623.
2 CONT * 4.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. IX, p. 624.
2 CONT * 5.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. IV, p. 422.
2 CONT * 6.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. XII/1, p. 462.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2682.htm#i80592
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *'''Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk 
2 CONT *'''M, #102999, b. 10 March 1536/37, d. 2 June 1572
2 CONT *'''     Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk was born on 10 March 1536/37. He was the son of Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey and Lady Frances de Vere.2 He married, firstly, Lady Mary Fitzalan, daughter of Henry Fitzalan, 19th Earl of 
2 CONC Arundel and Catherine Grey, on 30 March 1555. He married, secondly, Hon. Margaret Audley, daughter of Thomas Audley, 1st and last Baron Audley of Walden and Elizabeth Grey, in 1558.3 He married, thirdly, Elizabeth Leyburne, daught
2 CONC er of Sir James Leyburne, on 29 January 1566.4 He died on 2 June 1572 at age 35 at Tower Hill, The City, London, England, beheaded.2 He was also reported to have died on 30 September 1572. He was buried at Tower of London, The Cit
2 CONC y, London, England.
2 CONT *'''    Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk gained the title of 4th Duke of Norfolk in 1554. On 16 January 1572 he was attainted.5
2 CONT *'''Child of Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk and Lady Mary Fitzalan
2 CONT **Philip Howard, 20th Earl of Arundel+ b. 28 Jun 1557, d. 19 Oct 15955
2 CONT *'''Children of Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk and Hon. Margaret Audley
2 CONT **Margaret Howard+ b. a 1558
2 CONT **Thomas Howard, 1st Earl of Suffolk+ b. 24 Aug 1561, d. 20 May 16283
2 CONT **Lord William Howard+ b. 19 Dec 1563, d. 7 Oct 16406
2 CONT *Citations
