1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Howard,_1st_Earl_of_Northampton
2 CONT
2 CONT >"He was born at Shottesham, Norfolk, on 25 February 1540, the second son of Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey, the poet, and of his wife, the former Lady Frances de Vere, daughter of the 15th Earl of Oxford. He was the younger brother
2 CONC  of the 4th Duke of Norfolk, and uncle of Thomas Howard, Earl of Arundel. On the death of his father in 1547 he and his brother and sisters were entrusted to the care of his aunt, Mary FitzRoy, Duchess of Richmond and Somerset, wh
2 CONC o employed John Foxe as their tutor. With Foxe Howard remained at Reigate, a manor belonging to the Duke of Norfolk, throughout Edward VI's reign. On Mary's accession, the children's grandfather, the Duke of Norfolk, was released 
2 CONC from prison, and he dismissed Foxe".
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Reference'''
2 CONT
2 CONT  "Howard, Henry, Earl of Northampton". Dictionary of National Biography. London: Smith, Elder & Co. 1885–1900.
