1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Margaret Howard [1]
2 CONT *F, #103003, 
2 CONT *'''b. 30 January 1543, 
2 CONT *'''d. 17 March 1590/91
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Jul 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.07%
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Howard was born on 30 January 1543 at Lambeth, Surrey, England.[1] She was the daughter of Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey and Lady Frances de Vere.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She married Henry Scrope, 9th Lord Scrope of Bolton, son of John le Scrope, 8th Lord Scrope of Bolton and Lady Catherine Clifford, before 10 September 1565.[1 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She died on 17 March 1590/91 at age 48 at Carlisle, Cumberland, England.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From before 10 September 1565, her married name became Scrope. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Child of Margaret Howard and Henry Scrope, 9th Lord Scrope of Bolton
2 CONT *1. Thomas Scrope, 10th Lord Scrope of Bolton+1 b. c 1567, d. 2 Sep 1609
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XI, page 549. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S3409] Caroline Maubois, "re: Penancoet Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 2 December 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Penancoet Family."
2 CONT *From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Margaret Howard:
2 CONT *http://thepeerage.com/p10301.htm#i103003
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret Howard1
2 CONT *'''F, #61429, b. 30 January 1543, d. 17 March 1591
2 CONT *Father      Sir Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey1 b. bt 1516 - 1518, d. 19 Jan 1547
2 CONT *Mother     Frances Vere1 b. c 1517, d. 30 Jun 1577
2 CONT *'''     Margaret Howard was born on 30 January 1543 at Lambeth, England.1 She married Sir Henry Scrope, 9th Lord Scrope, son of John le Scrope, Baron Scrope of Bolton and Catherine Clifford, before 10 September 1565.1 Margaret Ho
2 CONC ward died on 17 March 1591 at Carlisle, Cumberlandshire, England, at age 48.1 She was buried on 8 June 1591 at Wensley, Yorkshire, England.1
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir Henry Scrope, 9th Lord Scrope b. c 1534, d. 13 Jun 1592
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. XI, p. 548-549.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2044.htm#i61429
2 CONT *________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret HOWARD (B. Scrope of Bolton)
2 CONT *'''Born: Jan 1542/3, Ashwell, Shropshire, England
2 CONT *'''Baptised: 30 Jan 1542/3, Lambeth, London, England
2 CONT *'''Died: 17 Mar 1591/2, Carlisle, Cumberland, England
2 CONT *'''Buried: 8 Jun 1592, Wensley, Lancashire, England
2 CONT *'''Notes: After her father’s execution for treason, she and her sisters, Jane and Catherine, were brought up by their aunt, Mary Howard, Duchess of Richmond. The girls were educated by John Foxe, who taught them Greek and Latin a
2 CONC nd had them compose poetry. It may be that Margaret Howard, unlike her older sisters, was permanently converted from the Catholicism of her father and grandfather to the Protestantism of her aunt. After Queen Mary succeeded to the
2 CONC  throne in 1553, Margaret was briefly in the household of her grandfather, Thomas Howard, 3rd Duke of Norfolk. Margaret married Henry Scrope, 9th baron Scrope of Bolton after his first wife died in Nov 1558. They had two sons, Tho
2 CONC mas, 10th baron Scrope, and Henry. When Mary Stuart first fled from Scotland into England her earliest prison was Carlisle Castle, where she was in the keeping of Lady Scrope. She was there by 18 May 1568 and was moved to Bolton C
2 CONC astle in Yorkshire by mid-Jul. On 3 Feb 1569, the Queen of Scots arrived at Tutbury Castle, where she was turned over to the keeping of the Earl of Shrewsbury. 
2 CONT *Father: Henry HOWARD (E. Surrey)
2 CONT *Mother: Frances De VERE (C. Surrey)
2 CONT *'''Married: Henry SCROPE (9° B. Scrope of Bolton) BEF 10 Sep 1565, Bolton, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Thomas SCROPE (10° B. Scrope of Bolton)
2 CONT **2. Henry SCROPE
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/HOWARD1.htm#Margaret HOWARD (B. Scrope of Bolton)
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey, KG (1516/1517 – 19 January 1547), was an English aristocrat, and one of the founders of English Renaissance poetry. He was a first cousin of Catherine Howard, the fifth wife of King Henry VIII.
2 CONT *He was the eldest son of Thomas Howard, 3rd Duke of Norfolk, and his second wife, the former Lady Elizabeth Stafford (daughter of Edward Stafford, 3rd Duke of Buckingham), so he was descended from kings on both sides of his famil
2 CONC y tree: King Edward I on his father's side and King Edward III on his mother's side. He was reared at Windsor with Henry VIII's illegitimate son Henry FitzRoy, 1st Duke of Richmond and Somerset, and they became close friends and, 
2 CONC later, brothers-in-law upon the marriage of Surrey's sister to Fitzroy.[1] Like his father and grandfather, he was a brave and able soldier, serving in Henry VIII's French wars as "Lieutenant General of the King on Sea and Land." 
2 CONC He was repeatedly imprisoned for rash behaviour, on one occasion for striking a courtier, on another for wandering through the streets of London breaking the windows of sleeping people.[2] He became Earl of Surrey in 1524 when his
2 CONC  grandfather died and his father became Duke of Norfolk.
2 CONT *In 1532 he accompanied his first cousin Anne Boleyn, the King, and the Duke of Richmond to France, staying there for more than a year as a member of the entourage of Francis I of France. In 1536 his first son, Thomas (later 4th D
2 CONC uke of Norfolk), was born, Anne Boleyn was executed on charges of adultery and treason, and the Duke of Richmond died at the age of 17 and was buried at one of the Howard homes, Thetford Abbey. In 1536 Surrey also served with his 
2 CONC father against the Pilgrimage of Grace rebellion protesting the Dissolution of the Monasteries.
2 CONT *He and his friend Sir Thomas Wyatt were the first English poets to write in the sonnet form that Shakespeare later used, and Surrey was the first English poet to publish blank verse (unrhymed Iambic pentameter) in his translation
2 CONC  of the second and fourth books of Virgil's Aeneid. Together, Wyatt and Surrey, due to their excellent translations of Petrarch's sonnets, are known as "Fathers of the English Sonnet". While Wyatt introduced the sonnet into Englis
2 CONC h, it was Surrey who gave them the rhyming meter and the division into quatrains that now characterizes the sonnets variously named English, Elizabethan or Shakespearean sonnets.[3][4]
2 CONT *Henry VIII, consumed by paranoia and increasing illness, became convinced that Surrey had planned to usurp the crown from his son Edward. The King had Surrey imprisoned—with his father—sentenced to death on 13 January 1547, and b
2 CONC eheaded for treason on 19 January 1547 (his father survived impending execution only by it being set for the day after the king happened to die, though he remained imprisoned). Surrey's son Thomas became heir to the Dukedom of Nor
2 CONC folk instead, inheriting it on the 3rd Duke's death in 1554.
2 CONT *He is buried in a spectacular painted alabaster tomb in the church of St Michael the Archangel, Framlingham.
2 CONT *He married Frances de Vere, the daughter of John de Vere, 15th Earl of Oxford, and Elizabeth Trussell. They had two sons and three daughters:
2 CONT ** Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk (10 March 1536 – 2 June 1572), married (1) Mary FitzAlan (2) Margaret Audley (3) Elizabeth Leyburne.
2 CONT ** Henry Howard, 1st Earl of Northampton, who died unmarried.
2 CONT ** Jane Howard, who married Charles Neville, 6th Earl of Westmorland.
2 CONT **''' Margaret Howard, who married Henry Scrope, 9th Baron Scrope of Bolton.
2 CONT ** Katherine Howard, who married Henry Berkeley, 7th Baron Berkeley.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Howard,_Earl_of_Surrey
2 CONT *________________
2 CONT *'''Henry Scrope, 9th Baron Scrope of Bolton, KG (c. 1534 – 13 June 1592) was the son and heir of John Scrope, 8th Baron Scrope of Bolton and Catherine Clifford, daughter of Henry Clifford, Earl of Cumberland.
2 CONT *Henry Scrope, a loyal supporter of Elizabeth I, was Marshal of the Army during the siege of Leith in 1559 which saw the end of the "Auld Alliance" between Scotland and France. He was appointed Warden of the West Marches and Capta
2 CONC in of Carlisle from c.1560 until 1591.
2 CONT *In April 1568 Mary, Queen of Scots fled across the Solway Firth to England after losing the Battle of Langside. She landed at Workington, travelling from there to Cockermouth and from thence to Carlisle. Scrope was at court at th
2 CONC e time, but hurried north with Sir Francis Knollys to take charge of her. After a brief imprisonment in Carlisle Castle Mary was moved with a large retinue of servants to Lord Scrope's home in Yorkshire, Bolton Castle. Six months 
2 CONC later she was moved on to Tutbury Castle.
2 CONT *In 1569, in the abortive Rising of the North, the Catholic Northern Earls rebelled with the objective of releasing Mary, Queen of Scots from her imprisonment at Tutbury and reinstating the old religion with Mary as queen. As Capt
2 CONC ain of Carlisle Scrope was involved in preventing the dissident Earls from marching into Scotland.[1] He was made a Knight of the Garter in 1584.
2 CONT *He died in Carlisle on June 13, 1592 and was succeeded by his eldest son Thomas Scrope, 10th Baron Scrope of Bolton. After his death in 1592 queen Elizabeth wrote a letter praising his loyal service.[2]
2 CONT *'''He married as his second wife Margaret Howard, daughter of Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey and Frances De Vere. They had two sons, the eldest of which was his heir, Thomas. His first wife was Mary, daughter of Edward North, 1st B
2 CONC aron North, who died in 1558. By her he had a daughter Mary, who married William Bowes of Streatlam.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_le_Scrope,_9th_Baron_Scrope_of_Bolton
2 CONT *_______________________________
2 CONT *Thomas le Scrope, 10th Baron Scrope of Bolton (1567 – 2 September 1609) was the son of '''Henry le Scrope, 9th Baron Scrope of Bolton and Margaret Howard''', daughter of Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey.
2 CONT *He was knight of the shire (MP) for Cumberland from 1584 to 1586 and from 1588 to 1593.[1]
2 CONT *He held the office of Warden of the English West March from 1593 until the Union of the Crowns of England and Scotland in 1603. He was made a Knight of the Garter in 1599.
2 CONT *While Scrope was Warden, the outlaw Kinmont Willie Armstrong was arrested (in violation of a truce day) and imprisoned at Carlisle Castle. Scrope had only recently been appointed to the post of Warden, and he was unsure of what t
2 CONC o do with an outlaw who had been illegally arrested. On 13 April 1596, as a result of a raid orchestrated by Walter Scott, 1st Lord Scott of Buccleuch, Kinmont Willie was freed. In a failed attempt to recapture Kinmont Willie, Scr
2 CONC ope "burnt the towns of Annan and Dumfries to the ground, capturing two hundred prisoners whom he marched home 'naked, chained together on leashes'. This caused a major diplomatic incident." [2]
2 CONT *He died at the village of Langar in Nottinghamshire, England in 1609. In 1584, he had married Philadelphia Carey, daughter of Henry Carey, 1st Baron Hunsdon and Ann Morgan. They had one child Emanuel Scrope, 1st Earl of Sunderlan
2 CONC d. In the village church at Langar is to be found a magnificent memorial to him. His tomb is adorned with an effigy of himself, his wife and their son Emmanuel.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Scrope,_10th_Baron_Scrope_of_Bolton
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Margaret Howard [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #103003, b. 30 January 1543, d. 17 March 1590/91 Last Edited=19 Jul 2011 Consanguinity Index=0.07% Margaret Howard was born on 30 January 1543 at Lambeth, Surrey, England.[1] She was the daughter of Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey
2 CONC  and Lady Frances de Vere.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Henry Scrope, 9th Lord Scrope of Bolton, son of John le Scrope, 8th Lord Scrope of Bolton and Lady Catherine Clifford, before 10 September 1565.[1 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 17 March 1590/91 at age 48 at Carlisle, Cumberland, England.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 10 September 1565, her married name became Scrope. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Margaret Howard and Henry Scrope, 9th Lord Scrope of Bolton
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Thomas Scrope, 10th Lord Scrope of Bolton+1 b. c 1567, d. 2 Sep 1609 Citations
