2 CONT From the Find A Grave page on Margaret Fiennes Lennard
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=33583487
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1540 - Monmouth, Wales
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Mar. 10, 1611 - Chevening, Kent, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Baroness Dacre, daughter of Thomas Fiennes, 9th Lord Dacre, and Mary Neville. Married the High Sheriff of Kent Sampson Lennard 16 Nov 1564 in Kent, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sampson and Lady Margaret's home was at Chevening, co. Kent, 15 miles southeast of London, until perhaps 1594, the year of her brother's death, after which they were much at Hurstmonceux Castle, which they greatly embellished and 
2 CONC where they entertained lavishly.
2 CONT
2 CONT At St. Botolph's Church at Chevening is the stately alabaster tomb of Sampson Lennard and Margaret Fiennes.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the south chancel, a stately tomb of alabaster, on which are the figures of a man in armour, and a lady in her robes, with their heads resting on cushions; at his feet is a brass head out of a ducal crown, and at her's a dog; o
2 CONC n the south side are three sons (Henry, George & Thomas) kneeling on cushions, the first in robes, the others in armour; on the north side are five daughters (Anne, Mary, Margaret, Elizabeth & Frances), erected for Sampson Lennard
2 CONC , esq. with his wife Margaret Fiences, lady Dacre, &c. obt. 1615; on the top are six coats of arms with their quarterings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *  Thomas Fiennes (1516 - 1541)
2 CONT *  Mary Neville Fiennes (1520 - 1565)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *  Sampson Lennard (1544 - 1615)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: St Botolph Churchyard, Chevening, Kent, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Sonnet Tidwell
2 CONT *Record added: Feb 06, 2009 
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 33583487
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Tomb of Margaret and Sampson Lennard, inside the chancel at Chevening Church. Sampson's effigy is beside Margaret's. The figures below are representations of their daughters, and on the opposite side are the sons. Photo taken 8/1/
2 CONC 2016.
2 CONT
