1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Mary Neville, Baroness le Despenser1
2 CONT *'''F, #14242, b. 25 March 1554, d. 28 June 1626
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.48%
2 CONT *'''     Mary Neville, Baroness le Despenser was born on 25 March 1554.1,2 She was the daughter''' of Sir Henry Neville, 4th Lord Abergavenny and Lady Frances Manners. '''She married Sir Thomas Fane''', son of George Fane and Joan
2 CONC  Waller, '''on 12 December 1574.1,2 She died on 28 June 1626 at age 72.2
2 CONT *'''      From before 1587, her married name became Fane.1 She succeeded to the title of 3rd Baroness le Despenser [E., 1314] on 25 May 1604, suo jure. She had claimed the succession to the Barony of Bergavenny, but this was settl
2 CONC ed on her cousin, Edward, and so the abeyance of the Barony of Le Despencer was terminated and awarded to Mary.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Mary Neville, Baroness le Despenser and Sir Thomas Fane
2 CONT **Francis Fane, 1st Earl of Westmorland+1 b. Feb 1579/80, d. 23 Mar 1628
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct
2 CONC  or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 34. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *[S8] BP1999 volume 1, page 17. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S8]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p1425.htm#i14242 ___________________
2 CONT *'''Mary NEVILLE (B. Despencer)
2 CONT *'''Born: 25 Mar 1554, Mereworth, Kent, England
2 CONT *'''Acceded: 1604
2 CONT *'''Died: 28 Jun 1626
2 CONT *'''Buried: 29 Jun 1626, Mereworth, Kent, England
2 CONT *'''Notes: The Complete Peerage vol.IV,p.283. She gained the title of Baroness Le Despencer on 25 May 1604, suo jure. She had claimed the succession to the Barony of Abergavenny, but this was settled on her cousin, Edward, and so 
2 CONC the abeyance of the Barony of Le Despencer was terminated and awarded to Mary.
2 CONT *Father: Henry NEVILLE (4° B. Abergavenny)
2 CONT *Mother: Frances MANNERS (B. Abergavenny)
2 CONT *'''Married: Thomas FANE (Sir) (b. 1538 - d. 1589) 12 Dec 1574, Birling, Kent, England
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Francis FANE (1° E. Westmoreland) (b. Feb 1579) (m. Mary Mildmay)
2 CONT **2. Frances FANE
2 CONT **3. George FANE
2 CONT **4. Thomas FANE
2 CONT **5. Edward FANE
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/NEVILLE4.htm#Mary NEVILLE (B. Despencer) ______________________
2 CONT *Henry Nevill, 6th and de jure 4th Baron Abergavenny K.B. (between 1527 and 1535 – 10 February 1587) was an English peer. He was the son of Sir George Nevill, 5th Baron Bergavenny, and Mary Stafford (daughter of Edward Stafford, 3
2 CONC rd Duke of Buckingham). He succeeded to the barony upon the death of his father, George Nevill, 5th Baron Bergavenny.
2 CONT *Henry, sixth (sometimes fourth) Lord Abergavenny, had summons to parliament on 23 January 1552, to 15 October 1586. He was one of the peers that sat in judgment on Mary, Queen of Scots, at Fotheringay. He died at his seat called 
2 CONC Comfort, near Birling, Kent, on 10 February 1587.
2 CONT *He married first, Frances, daughter of Thomas Manners, 1st Earl of Rutland; he married secondly, Elizabeth, daughter of Stephen Darell, of Spelmonden, Kent (she remarried to Sir William Sedley, of Southfleet, Kent, Knt. and Bart.
2 CONC ); by his first wife, he had an '''only daughter Mary Neville who married Sir Thomas Fane.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *'''Mary Neville, Baroness le Despencer, died 28 June 1626, aged 72, buried at Mereworth, Kent, having married at Birling, 12 December 1574, as second wife, to Thomas Fane (d 1589), of Badsell, Kent[11] (whose son''', Francis, was
2 CONC  created Earl of Westmorland), knighted at Dover Castle, 26 August 1573, died 13 March 1589, '''w.d. 12 March 1589, pd. 10 February 1590. Lady Fane claimed the barony of Abergavenny against Edward Nevill, the heir male upon whom t
2 CONC he castle of Bergavenny was settled as aforesaid, and as a compromise, she was by letters patent, 25 May 1604, confirmed in the name, style, and dignity of Baroness le Despencer, to the heirs of her body, with the ancient seat, pl
2 CONC ace, and precedence of her ancestors.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Nevill,_6th_Baron_Bergavenny _________________
2 CONT *	le Despencer, Baron (E, 1295 with precedency from 1264)
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *1d. Henry [Nevill], 4th and 6th Baron Bergavenny (dspm. 10 Feb 1586/7), mar. (1) bef. 31 Jan 1555/6 Lady Frances Manners (bur. Sep 1576), 3rd dau. of Thomas [Manners], 1st Earl of Rutland, by his second wife Eleanor Paston, dau. 
2 CONC of Sir William Paston, of Paston, co. Norfolk, and (2) Elizabeth Darrell (mar. (2) Sir William Sedley, 1st Bt., of Southfleet, co. Kent;  d. aft. Feb 1601/2), dau. and cohrss. of Stephen Darrell, of Spelmonden, in Horsmonden, co. 
2 CONC Kent, Chief Clerk of the Royal Kitchen, by his wife Philippa Weldon, dau. of Edward Weldon, Clerk of the Green Cloth, and had issue by his first wife:
2 CONT **'''	1e. Hon Mary Nevill, de jure suo jure Baroness Bergavenny later suo jure Baroness la Despencer
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *On the death of the infant Lady Anne Beauchamp, in her own right Countess of Warwick and Baroness Burghersh, the Barony of Burghersh and the representation of the three Baronies of le Despencer fell into abeyance between her cous
2 CONC in George [Nevill], Lord Bergavenny, and her aunt Anne, Countess of Warwick. On the attainder and execution of Lady Margaret Plantagenet, in her own right Countess of Warwick and Salisbury, on 28 May 1541 any claim to the four Bar
2 CONC onies by the descendants of Anne, Countess of Warwick, lapsed and the sole representation lay with the Barons Bergavenny. The attainder of Thomas, Earl of Gloucester, was reversed in 1461 but the abeyancies continued until 25 May 
2 CONC 1604, when the abeyancy of the 1295 Barony of le Despencer was terminated '''in favour of Mary, Lady Fane:
2 CONT *
2 CONT *'''Hon Mary Nevill later Fane, de jure suo jure Baroness Bergavenny later suo jure Baroness la Despencer
2 CONT *'''born  25 Mar 1554
2 CONT *'''mar.  12 Dec 1574 as his second wife Sir Thomas Fane, of Badsell, co. Kent (d. 13 Mar 1588/9)
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	1. Hon Francis Fane, later 1st Earl of Westmorland later 7th Baron le Despencer
2 CONT *'''died  28 Jun 1626
2 CONT *'''suc. by  son
2 CONT *
2 CONT *Francis [Fane], 1st Earl of Westmorland later 7th Baron le Despencer
2 CONT *born	Feb 1579/80
2 CONT *mar.	aft. 15 Feb 1598/9 Mary Mildmay (b. c. 1582; d. 9 Apr 1640), only surv. dau. and hrss. of Sir Anthony Mildmay, of Apethorpe, co. Northampton, by his wife Grace Sherrington, dau. and cohrss. of Sir Henry Sherrington, of Lacoc
2 CONC k, co. Wiltshire
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	.... etc.
2 CONT *died	23 Mar 1628/9
2 CONT *created	29 Dec 1624 Baron Burghersh and Earl of Westmorland
2 CONT *suc. by	son
2 CONT *note	Member of Parliament for Kent 1601, for Maidstone 1604-11, 1614 and 1620-22 and for Peterborough 1624; Knight of the Bath at the Coronation of King James I 1603; a Commissioner to preserve the King's game in Northamptonshire
2 CONC , Huntingdonshire and Rutland 1620; suc. his mother 28 Jun 1626 as 8th Baron le Despencer as well as 6th and 8th Baron Bergavenny
2 CONT * .... etc. 
2 CONT *From: http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/despencer1295.htm?zoom_highlight=fane _______________________________
2 CONT *	(A)bergavenny, Baron (E, 1450 - abeyant 1762)
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Henry [Nevill], 4th and 6th Baron Bergavenny
2 CONT *born
2 CONT *mar. (1)	bef. 31 Jan 1555/6 Lady Frances Manners (bur. Sep 1576), 3rd dau. of Thomas [Manners], 1st Earl of Rutland, by his second wife Eleanor Paston, dau. of Sir William Paston, of Paston, co. Norfolk
2 CONT *'''only child by first wife
2 CONT **'''	1. Hon Mary Nevill, de jure suo jure Baroness Bergavenny later suo jure Baroness la Despencer
2 CONT *mar. (2)	Elizabeth Darrell (mar. (2) Sir William Sedley, 1st Bt., of Southfleet, co. Kent;  d. aft. Feb 1601/2), dau. and cohrss. of Stephen Darrell, of Spelmonden, in Horsmonden, co. Kent, Chief Clerk of the Royal Kitchen, by hi
2 CONC s wife Philippa Weldon, dau. of Edward Weldon, Clerk of the Green Cloth
