2 CONT **	(f) '''Sir Thomas Fane, of Badsell, Kent, Lord Warden of the Cinque Ports, Governor of Dover Castle, and Sheriff of Kent 14th Elizabeth ; married Mary Neville, Baroness Despencer, her son''' Francis Fane Baron Despencer, was cr
2 CONC eated Baron Burghersh and Earl of Westmoreland 29th December, 1624. Sir Thomas Scott was connected with the Fane family by the marriage of his son-in-law, Anthony St. Leger, whose mother, Ursula, was daughter of George Neville, Ea
2 CONC rl of Abergavenny, a near kinsman of Sir Thomas Fane and the Earl of Westmoreland his son. (See note, p. vii. ] 
