1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Primary Sources
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000038366633489& Will] of Katherine, Lady Windsor, of Hewell, late wife of Edward, Lord Windsor, dated 14 February 1598 and proved 24 April 1600
2 CONT
2 CONT Family members mentioned: <br/>
2 CONT   "my son Frederick" deceased<br/>
2 CONT   "my eldest son Henry, Lord Windsor"<br/>
2 CONT   "my son Edward"<br/>
2 CONT   "my son Andrew"<br/>
2 CONT   "my daughter Margaret"<br/>
2 CONT   "my daughter Katherine"<br/>
2 CONT   "my daughter[-in-law] Anne Windsor"<br/>
2 CONT   "my daughter[-in-law] Elizabeth Windsor"
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography
2 CONT KATHERINE de VERE (c.1541-January 17, 1600)
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine de Vere was the daughter of John de Vere, 16th earl of Oxford (1512-August 3, 1562) and his first wife, Dorothy Neville (1515-c. January 1548). On February 1, 1548, while still a child, she was promised in marriage to th
2 CONC e duke of Somerset's son, Henry Seymour, age seven. This marriage contract was cancelled after Somerset's execution. Katherine instead married Edward, 3rd baron Windsor (1532-January 24, 1575) and was the mother of 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Frederick, 4th baron (February 2, 1559-December 24, 1585),   
2 CONT # Henry, 5th baron (August 10, 1562-April 6, 1605),   
2 CONT # Andrew (d.1598+),  
2 CONT # Edward (d.1598+),   
2 CONT # William (1566-before 1598),   
2 CONT # Catherine (c.1567-December 15, 1640), and   
2 CONT # Margaret (d.1598+).   
2 CONT
2 CONT On her father’s death, Katherine brought suit against her half brother, claiming that his mother’s marriage to her father had not been valid because there had been a precontract between her father and Katherine’s lady-in-waiting, 
2 CONC Dorothy Fosser. Her will, written February 14, 1598, can be found at Oxford-Shakespeare.com. She died at Hewell in Worcestershire and was buried at Tardebigge. Portraits: alone, 1567; with her family, 1568; both by the Master of t
2 CONC he Countess of Warwick
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: [http://www.kateemersonhistoricals.com/TudorWomenU-V.htm Tudor Women]
