1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ursula STAFFORD
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: ABT 1553, Bobbing Court, Kent, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: Richard Drake obtained a Court appointment as Equerry to Queen Elizabeth in 1577, and bought an estate in Esher. He received a ransom of 2,500 pounds for a distinguished Spanish prisoner who was captured after the defeat of
2 CONC  the Armada and housed with Richard Drake for four-and-a half years until his exchange with an English prisoner in the hands of the Spaniards. The family of Drake of Shardeloes in Buckinghamshire are descendants of this Richard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: William STAFFORD of Grafton (Sir)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Dorothy STAFFORD
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Richard DRAKE (Esq.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Francis DRAKE
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STAFFORD2.htm#Ursula STAFFORD1
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *The Prominent Families of the United States of America By Arthur Meredyth Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=3-78JbUTUewC&pg=PA58&lpg=PA58&dq=John+Drake+1628&source=bl&ots=g8L45QYWVp&sig=Xx44eoPm0nheurl4beQBIFB8czU&hl=en&ei=9FrrTLHGD4a4sQPCo4n2Dg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=9&ved=0CDAQ6AEwCA#v=o
2 CONC nepage&q=John%20Drake%201628&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.57
2 CONT *JOHN DRAKE ( -1558), of Ashe, Co. Devon ; High Sheriff of Devon ; m., 1535, Amye, dau. of Roger Grenville, of Stowe, Cornwall, and, by her (who d. 18 Feb. 1577, and was bur. at Musbury), left issue: --
2 CONT *1. Bernard, of whom later.
2 CONT *2. Robert, of Wiscombe Park; m. Elizabeth, dau. of Humphrey Prideaux, of Theoborough, and had issue.
2 CONT *3. ''''''RICHARD, and equerry to Queen Elizabeth; m. URSULA, dau. of Sir William STAFFORD, Knt.; d. 1633, leaving issue.
2 CONT *He d. 4 Oct. 1558.
2 CONT *<nowiki>--------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *A genealogical and heraldic history of the extinct and dormant baronetcies ... By John Burke, Sir Bernard Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=DjIGAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA168&lpg=PA168&dq=John+Drake+1628&source=bl&ots=scEsfRjKQA&sig=7EmGMIcad0Vuzk0R8P944q0y7ps&hl=en&ei=4hvrTIamDYGCsQPB1IHaDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CCEQ6AEwBDgK
2 CONC #v=onepage&q=Tothill&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.167
2 CONT *John Drake, esq. of Ashe, who m. Anne, daughter of Roger Grenville, esq. of Stowe, in Cornwall, and left at his decease, 4th October, 1558, Bernard (Sir), his successor.
2 CONT *Robert, of Wiscomb, in the parish of Southlegh, Devon, m. Elizabeth, daughter of Humphrey Prideaux, of Thewborough, by whom, with other issue, he had Robert and Henry, the former a colonel in the Netherlands, of great esteem with
2 CONC  the Prince of Orange and the States General, and the latter a captain in the army, both killed in the prime of life in the defence of Ostend.
2 CONT *''''''RICHARD, ancestor of the Drakes of Shardeloes.
2 CONT *..........
2 CONT *The youngest son,
2 CONT *''''''RICHARD DRAKE, esq. one of the equerries to Queen Elizabeth, m. URSULA, daugher of Sir William STAFFORD, knt. and dying 11 July, 1603, was s. by his son,
2 CONT *Francis Drake, esq. of Esher, one of the gentlemen of the privy chamber in ordinary, who wedded Joan, daughter of William Tothill, esq. of Shardeloes, in Bucks, and had issue.
2 CONT *<nowiki>------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry, Volume 1 By John Burke
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=YdIKAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA347&lpg=PA347&dq=John+Drake+1628&source=bl&ots=qCCjm0cd2J&sig=8uP4B--se2OMstpQBzWnECMlANg&hl=en&ei=4hvrTIamDYGCsQPB1IHaDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CBgQ6AEwATgK
2 CONC #v=onepage&q=John%20Drake%201628&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.347
2 CONT *John Drake, Esq. of Ashe, who s. his father in the representation of the family, m. (26 HENRY VIII.,) Amye, dau. of Roger Grenville, Esq. of Stow, co. Cornwall, and had issue,
2 CONT *I Bernard, his heir.
2 CONT *II. Robert, of Wiscomb Park, in the parish of South Legh, m. Elizabeth, dau. of Humphrey Prideaux, Esq. of Theoborough, and had issue seven son and three daus.,
2 CONT *III. ''''''RICHARD, equerry to Queen Elizabeth, m. URSULA, dau. of Sir William STAFFORD, Knt., and from whom the Drakes of Shardeloes.
2 CONT *Mr. Drake, who served the office of sheriff for the county of Devon, 4 Queen Elizabeth, d. 4 Oct. 1558, and was s. by his son, ..................
2 CONT *Pg.348
2 CONT *TYRWHITT-DRAKE OF SHARDELOES.
2 CONT *RICHARD DRAKE, Esq., third son of John Drake, Esq. of Ashe, by Amye, his wife, dau. of Roger Grenville, Esq., of Stowe, was one of the equerries to Queen Elizabeth. He m. URSULA, dau. of Sir William STAFFORD, Knt, and dying 11 Ju
2 CONC ly 1603, was s. by his son,
2 CONT *Francis Drake, Esq. of Esher, on of the gentlemen of the privy chamber in ordinary, who m. Joan, dau. of William Tothill, Esq. of Shardeloes, in the co. of Buckingham, and had issue, William, his heir; John, who d. unm. in 1623; 
2 CONC Francis, of Walton-on-Thames; and Joan. Mr. Drake d. 17 Mar, 1633, and was s. by his eldest son,
2 CONT *<nowiki>---------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *Genealogical and personal memoirs relating to the families of the ..., Volume 1 edited by William Richard Cutter, William Frederick Adams
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=kmujIJi3_FkC&pg=PA234&lpg=PA234&dq=John+Drake+1628&source=bl&ots=asI01_283m&sig=SmFh_HCFkQYu4mtRGXvbScaj9sI&hl=en&ei=CxbrTK-GJY3CsAOe7v2LDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0CCcQ6AEwBQ#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=John%20Drake%201628&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.234
2 CONT *(VI) John Drake, of Mount Drake, Ashe and Exmouth, was son and heir, and high sheriff of Devon in the time of Queen Elizabeth. He married, in 1535, Amye, daughter of Roger Greenville, of Stow. He died October 4, 1558, and he and 
2 CONC his wife are buried in the parish church at Musbury, where may be seen their tomb, bearing their effigies. She died February 18, 1577. Children: 1. Sir Barnard, knight; mentioned below. 2. Robert of Wiscomb; married Elizabeth Prid
2 CONC eaux. 3. RICHARD of Esher, born 1535, equerry to Queen Elizabeth; married URSULA STAFFORD; died July 11, 1603.
2 CONT *<nowiki>-----------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ursula Stafford
2 CONT * Born: Abt 1557, Esher, Surrey, England
2 CONT * Marriage: Robert Drake
2 CONT
2 CONT Ursula married Robert Drake, son of John Drake and Anne Grenville. (Robert Drake was born in 1528 in Wiscombe, Devonshire England, died on 30 Mar 1600 in Wiscombe Park, Southleigh, Devonshire England and was buried on 30 Mar 1660 
2 CONC in Wiscombe, Devonshire England.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.heapgen.org/hp/1742.htm
