2 CONT *Notes: '''Mary Beaumont''' was created Countess of Buckingham in her own right on 1 Jul 1618. As a young woman, Mary was a waiting gentlewoman in the household of Lady Beaumont of Cole Orton, but by her first marriage, to Sir Geo
2 CONC rge Villiers of Brooksby, Leicestershire (d. Jan 1606), she had four successful children: John, Viscount Purbeck (b. ABT 1591 - d. 1657); George, Duke of Buckingham (b. 1592 - d. 1628), King James I's favorite; Christopher, Earl o
2 CONC f Anglesey (b. 1593 - d. 1630), and Susan, Countess of Denbigh (b. ABT 1591 - d. 1655). Mary lived at Goadby with her children '''after Villiers's death but married twice more''', first on 19 Jun 1606 to eighty-year-old Sir Willia
2 CONC m Rayner of Orton Longueville, Hertfordshire (d. Nov 1606), '''and second to Sir Thomas Compton. The last marriage was unhappy, as Sir Thomas was impoverished and rarely sober'''. The Countess was buried in Westminster Abbey.
