1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Somerset re-married (2nd) before 1567 Theophila Newton, daughter of John Newton (otherwise Cradock), Knt., of East Harptree, Somerset, by Margaret, daughter of Anthony Poyntz, Knt. A portrait of Countess Th
2 CONC eophila by an unknown artist of that date is mentioned by Ashelford, Visual History of Costume (1983): 72. Theophila survived him and is said to have married (2) William Paratt, of Pantglas.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William died "at his house at Hackney 21 Feb. 1588/9, and was buried at Raglan Monmoughshire. He left a will proved 7 Nov. 1589."[1]
