2 CONT He was first married by contract of 4 August 1627 to Claude Dupuy. Ten days later he acquired by purchase, (not inheritence from his father who never owned it) the property known as la Massicotterie.[1] He passed away in November 
2 CONC 1648. His second wife and widow Louise de Marle was remarried in 1649.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine was only three years old when her father died in the fall of 1648.
