1 CONT [edit] Portrayals in fiction
1 CONT
1 CONT Edward is a character in the play Richard III by William Shakespeare. He has been played on film and television by:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Kathleen Yorke in the silent short Richard III (1911), dramatising a part of Shakespeare's play
1 CONT     * Howard Stuart in the silent Shakespeare adaptation Richard III (1912)
1 CONT     * Ronald Sinclair in Tower of London (1939), a horror film loosely dramatising the rise to power of Richard III
1 CONT     * Paul Huson in Richard III, with Laurence Olivier
1 CONT     * Hugh Janes in the BBC series An Age of Kings (1960), which contained all the history plays from Richard II to Richard III
1 CONT     * Eugene Martin in the remake of Tower of London (1962)
1 CONT     * Nicolaus Haenel in the West German TV version of Shakespeare's play König Richard III (1964)
1 CONT     * Jonathan Soper in the "Who Killed the Princes in the Tower?" episode of the BBC drama documentary series Second Verdict (1976)
1 CONT     * Dorian Ford in the BBC Shakespeare version of The Tragedy of Richard the Third (1983)
1 CONT     * Spike Hood (voice) in the BBC series Shakespeare: The Animated Tales (1994)
1 CONT     * Marco Williamson in Richard III (1995), with Ian McKellen as Richard
1 CONT     * Timotei Cresta in the British television drama Princes in the Tower (2005)
1 CONT     * Jon Plummer in Richard III (2005), a modernised version set on a Brighton housing estate
1 CONT     * Germaine De Leon in Richard III (2007), a modern day version
1 CONT
