1 CONT
1 CONT MARGARET WYDEVILLE, illegitimate daughter by Gwenllian Stradling.  She married before 1480 ROBERT POYNTZ, Knt., of Iron Acton, Gloucestershire, Esquire of the Body to King Edward IV, Sheriff of Gloucestershire, Deputy and Lieutena
1 CONC nt of the Port of Bristol, Steward of Barton Hundred, Seneschal of Berkeley Castle, Chancelor and Privy Councillor to Queen Katherine of Aragon, son and heir of John Poyntz, Esq., of Iron Acton, Gloucestershire, by Alice, daughter
1 CONC  of ____ Cox (or Cocks), of Bristol.  They had six sons ... and four daughters ....  He was knighted at the Battle of Redmore 22 August 1485.  He was present at the Coronation of Elizabeth, Queen Consort of King Henry VII in 1486.
1 CONC   In 1520 he was present at the Field of the Cloth of Gold.  SIR ROBERT POYNTZ died testate ... 5 Nov. 1520, and was buried in Gaunt Chapel beside Bristol.  His wife, Margaret, predeceased him.
0 @N6000000002322303960@ NOTE A gifted humanist prince, Ferdinand was loved by the people, who
1 CONT affectionately addressed him in the diminutive Ferrandino. He became king
1 CONT upon the abdication of his father as French forces approached northern Italy.
1 CONT In the following month, the French captured Naples and Ferdinand fled to
1 CONT Sicily. Aided by a Spanish army and the Venetian fleet, he recovered almost
1 CONT all his lands by the summer of 1496 and was received triumphantly by the
1 CONT populace. His sudden death, however, opened the door to Spanish usurpation.
