0 @N6000000003658810266@ NOTE From Dictionary of National Biography:
1 CONT
1 CONT SIR ANTHONY POYNTZ (1480?-1533) inherited Iron Acton, where his descendants were seated for many generations.  He was knighted in 1513, when he commanded a ship in Howard's expedition against France.  In September 1518 he was sent
1 CONC  on an embassy to the French king, and was present at the Field of the Cloth of Gold in July 1502.  In 1521 he was one of the jury at Bristol before whom the Duke of Buckingham was indicted.  In 1522 he joined in Surrey's expediti
1 CONC on to Francis in command of the Santa Maria.  In the following year he became vice-admiral, and was employed in command of some twelve or fourteen sail in preventing the return of Albany to Scotland.  In 1523 he was administrator 
1 CONC for his father.  In 1527 he served as a sheriff of Gloucestershire, and in 1530 was on a commission to inquire into Wolsey's possessions.  He died in 1533, having married, first, Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Huddlesfield; an
1 CONC d secondly, Joan, widow of Sir Richard Guilford.  His eldest son, Sir Nicholas, born in 1510, was a prominent courtier during the latter part of Henry VIII's reign, and died in 1557.  A portrait of Sir Nicholas by Holbein belongs 
1 CONC to the Marquis of Bristol, and two drawings, also attributed to Holbein, to her majesty the queen. ... Another, which is anonymous, belonged in 1866 to the Marquis of Ormonde.
1 CONT
1 CONT From Magna Carta Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT ELIZABETH HUDDESFIELD, married (1st) ANTHONY POYNTZ, Knt., of Iron Acton, Gloucestershire, Sheriff of Gloucestershire, son and heir of Robert Poyntz, Knt., of Iron Acton, Gloucestershire, by Margaret, illegitimate daughter of Anth
1 CONC ony Wydeville, Knt., K.G., 2nd Earl Rivers, 8th Lord Scales. ... He was born about 1480 (aged 40 in 1520).  They had five sons ... and two daughters. ... Anthony and Elizabeth were both legatees in the 1510 will of her mother, Kat
1 CONC herine Huddesfield.  In 1513 he was one of the captains in a fleet of 42 ships which assembled at Portsmouth under the command of Thomas Howard, Lord High Admiral.  He married (2nd) JOAN _____, widow of Richard Guildford, Knt.  SI
1 CONC R ANTHONY POYNTZ died intestate in 1535.
