1 CONC t of her life, although Wardour was not included .Even after 1554 when Mary Tudor(Mary I, a Catholic ruled 1553- 1558)had fully restored status to Sir Thomas'son, Matthew- 13 more years were to pass before any steps were taken to 
1 CONC recover Wardour. Sir Matthew married Margaret Willoughby, (Cousin to Lady Jane Grey, who was Queen for nine days before Mary I. Lady Jane Grey was beheaded.)"Sir Matthew's years at Wardour extended to almost the close of Elizabeth
1 CONC  the Ist reign. (Her reign was from 1558 to 1603)Sir Matthew was naturally a frequent visitor at court.During the time Sir Matthew was at home at Wardour, his son Thomas, who was later to become the first Lord Arundell, was campai
1 CONC gning abroad. It is sufficient to say that his part in this crusade brought him the title of Count of The Holy Roman Empire. It is typical of Elizabeth I that she caused Thomas Arundell to be clapped in the Tower on his return for
1 CONC  daring to accept this foreign title."
