1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Mary I
1 CONT Queen of England and Ireland, Queen Consort of Aragon, Castile, and Naples, Consort of the Spanish Netherlands. (more...)
1 CONT Queen Mary I of Englandpainted in 1554 by Antonius MorMuseum of Prado, Madrid
1 CONT Queen Mary I of England
1 CONT painted in 1554 by Antonius Mor
1 CONT Museum of Prado, Madrid
1 CONT Reign 19 July 1553–17 November 1558
1 CONT Coronation 1 October 1553
1 CONT Predecessor Jane de facto;
1 CONT Edward VI de jure
1 CONT Successor Elizabeth I
1 CONT Consort Philip II of Spain
1 CONT Royal house Tudor
1 CONT Father Henry VIII
1 CONT Mother Catherine of Aragon
1 CONT Born 18 February 1516(1516-02-18)
1 CONT Palace of Placentia, Greenwich
1 CONT Died 17 November 1558 (aged 42)
1 CONT Saint James's Palace, London
1 CONT Burial 14 December 1558
1 CONT Westminster Abbey, London
1 CONT
1 CONT Mary I (18 February 1516 – 17 November 1558), was Queen of England and Queen of Ireland from 19 July 1553 until her death. The fourth crowned monarch of the Tudor dynasty, she is remembered for restoring England to Roman Catholici
1 CONC sm after succeeding her short-lived brother, Edward VI, to the English throne. In the process, she had almost three hundred religious dissenters burned at the stake in the Marian Persecutions, resulting in her being called Bloody 
1 CONC Mary. Her re-establishment of Roman Catholicism was reversed by her successor and half-sister, Elizabeth I.
1 CONT Contents
